e":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-config#remote","content":"Remote hosts are added in the web UI under **Settings** › **Remote hosts**, or with `mizuoto remote add`, which also checks that the host answers.","locale":"en"},"11123":{"id":"/en/docs/cli","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Mizuoto Documentation","Command line"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli","locale":"en"},"11124":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-0","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli","content":"The mizuoto command line calls the same core as the web UI and the HTTP API: this page covers its shared conventions, foreground jobs, exit codes, and using it while a server runs.","locale":"en"},"11125":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-1","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#the-commands","content":"The commands","locale":"en"},"11126":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-2","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#how-it-differs-from-the-web-ui","content":"How it differs from the web UI","locale":"en"},"11127":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-3","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"Output and `--json`","locale":"en"},"11128":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-4","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Exit codes","locale":"en"},"11129":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-5","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#debugging-and-logs","content":"Debugging and logs","locale":"en"},"11130":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-6","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"Using it while a server runs","locale":"en"},"11131":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-7","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#common-workflows","content":"Common workflows","locale":"en"},"11132":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-8","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#check-the-engines-download-a-model-speak","content":"Check the engines, download a model, speak","locale":"en"},"11133":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-9","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#clone-and-design-voices","content":"Clone and design voices","locale":"en"},"11134":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-10","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#hear-it-as-it-is-made","content":"Hear it as it is made","locale":"en"},"11135":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-11","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#batches-and-parameters","content":"Batches and parameters","locale":"en"},"11136":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-12","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#transcribe-convert-and-edit","content":"Transcribe, convert and edit","locale":"en"},"11137":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-13","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#training","content":"Training","locale":"en"},"11138":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-14","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#projects","content":"Projects","locale":"en"},"11139":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-15","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-completion","content":"Shell completion","locale":"en"},"11140":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-16","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#next","content":"Next","locale":"en"},"11141":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-17","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli","content":"The `mizuoto` command line does what the web UI does: speak, clone and design voices, convert and edit recordings, transcribe, check torch and the engines, manage models, presets, projects, datasets and training, remote hosts, jobs and settings. It is a thin wrapper: each command parses its arguments, calls the **one** core method for that operation and prints the result. The HTTP API behind the web UI calls the same methods, so both behave alike, and the records `--json` prints have the same shape as the API's JSON.","locale":"en"},"11142":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-18","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli","content":"This page covers the shared conventions and common workflows; every command's options are in the Command reference, settings and environment variables in Configuration and environment variables.","locale":"en"},"11143":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-19","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#the-commands","content":"Add `--help` at any level; a group name alone (such as `mizuoto model`) shows that group's help too. Every level accepts `--debug`.","locale":"en"},"11144":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-20","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#how-it-differs-from-the-web-ui","content":"**Jobs run in the foreground.** `speak`, `design`, `model download`, `train run`, `project render` and the like create a job and run it in the terminal until it ends; a progress bar goes to stderr (only when stderr is a terminal, and not with `--json`), with bytes, speed and time left for downloads.","locale":"en"},"11145":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-21","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#how-it-differs-from-the-web-ui","content":"**Ctrl+C cancels the job.** The job is marked **Cancelled**, the engine stops at its next check (the next token or step), a training stage's process is stopped, and the command exits with code 130.","locale":"en"},"11146":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-22","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#how-it-differs-from-the-web-ui","content":"**No server needed.** Each command opens the data folder (settings, database, models) itself and closes it when done; the engines run in the command's own process and the models it loaded go with it, so every `speak` loads its model again. For many sentences in a row, a server (the web UI or the HTTP API) is faster: it keeps models loaded.","locale":"en"},"11147":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-23","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#how-it-differs-from-the-web-ui","content":"**Any path works.** The web UI reads server files only inside **Folders the browser may open** (`paths.browse_roots`); `--ref`, `model import`, `dataset import` and the like take any path on this machine.","locale":"en"},"11148":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-24","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"List and info commands print tables; with `--json` they print JSON in the shape of the matching API record, for scripts:","locale":"en"},"11149":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-25","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"A few details:","locale":"en"},"11150":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-26","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"`speak` prints each result's path, duration and sample rate. Results are always kept in the outputs folder (and appear in **History**); `-o` also copies one to the path you give, whose extension picks the format.","locale":"en"},"11151":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-27","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"`speak --json` prints `{\"job\": …, \"outputs\": […]}`: the finished job and the output records it made.","locale":"en"},"11152":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-28","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"`speak --plan` checks the request and prints the plan (model, device, voice mode, segments, parameters) without running anything.","locale":"en"},"11153":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-29","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"Warnings (such as dropped parameters the model does not take) go to stderr, starting with `warning:`, never into stdout.","locale":"en"},"11154":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-30","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A failing command prints the error and, when the error names a fix, the command to run on the next line; the exit code tells the kind of error. The codes are defined in `mizuoto/core/codes.py`, each error class's exit code in `mizuoto/core/errors.py`:","locale":"en"},"11155":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-31","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Exit code","locale":"en"},"11156":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-32","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Error code","locale":"en"},"11157":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-33","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Typical cause","locale":"en"},"11158":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-34","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"0","locale":"en"},"11159":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-35","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Success","locale":"en"},"11160":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-36","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"1","locale":"en"},"11161":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-37","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`internal_error`","locale":"en"},"11162":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-38","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"An unclassified internal error; answering \"no\" to a confirmation","locale":"en"},"11163":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-39","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"2","locale":"en"},"11164":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-40","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`not_found`","locale":"en"},"11165":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-41","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Unknown model, voice, job, output or engine. Click also exits with 2 for command-line mistakes (unknown option, value out of range)","locale":"en"},"11166":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-42","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"3","locale":"en"},"11167":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-43","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`conflict`, `busy`","locale":"en"},"11168":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-44","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A name exists already; a stage is running; `webui` finds no free port","locale":"en"},"11169":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-45","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"4","locale":"en"},"11170":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-46","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`invalid_input`, `invalid_path`, `capability_not_supported`, `parameter_not_supported`, `parameter_out_of_range`, `reference_invalid`, `language_not_supported`","locale":"en"},"11171":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-47","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"An invalid request: the model lacks that voice mode or parameter, a reference clip is too short or too long, an unsupported language; `webui`'s certificate file is missing","locale":"en"},"11172":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-48","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"5","locale":"en"},"11173":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-49","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`licence_not_accepted`","locale":"en"},"11174":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-50","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A licence-gated engine (Fish Speech, IndexTTS) whose licence is not accepted yet","locale":"en"},"11175":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-51","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"7","locale":"en"},"11176":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-52","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`model_missing`, `engine_not_installed`, `asset_missing`","locale":"en"},"11177":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-53","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A model not downloaded; a package the engine needs is not installed (torch, or a licence-gated engine's `mizuoto-fishspeech` / `mizuoto-indextts`); a shared asset missing","locale":"en"},"11178":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-54","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"8","locale":"en"},"11179":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-55","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`device_unavailable`","locale":"en"},"11180":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-56","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A device that does not exist or cannot be used, such as a device naming an unknown remote host","locale":"en"},"11181":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-57","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"9","locale":"en"},"11182":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-58","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`compute_unavailable`","locale":"en"},"11183":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-59","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"No usable device, or not enough free GPU memory (`detail.reason` is `out_of_memory` or `no_device`)","locale":"en"},"11184":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-60","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"10","locale":"en"},"11185":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-61","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`worker_failed`, `engine_error`","locale":"en"},"11186":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-62","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A training stage's process or a remote agent died or stopped answering; the engine raised an exception","locale":"en"},"11187":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-63","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"11","locale":"en"},"11188":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-64","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`timeout`","locale":"en"},"11189":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-65","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"An operation took too long","locale":"en"},"11190":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-66","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"12","locale":"en"},"11191":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-67","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`download_failed`","locale":"en"},"11192":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-68","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A file could not be downloaded from any source","locale":"en"},"11193":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-69","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"14","locale":"en"},"11194":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-70","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`remote_unavailable`","locale":"en"},"11195":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-71","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A remote host cannot be reached, refused the token, or speaks another protocol version","locale":"en"},"11196":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-72","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"130","locale":"en"},"11197":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-73","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`cancelled`","locale":"en"},"11198":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-74","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Ctrl+C, or the job was cancelled","locale":"en"},"11199":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-75","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"A missing package looks like this:","locale":"en"},"11200":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-76","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#debugging-and-logs","content":"`MIZUOTO_LOG_LEVEL` sets the log level as well (`DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING`, `ERROR`; default `INFO`). Each job's full log is `jobs/<job id>.log` in the data folder (`mizuoto job log <job id>`); a training stage's output goes into its job's log too.","locale":"en"},"11201":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-77","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"The command line and a server can open the same data folder at the same time. They are separate processes sharing the settings file, the database and the folders:","locale":"en"},"11202":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-78","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"**Settings**: `mizuoto config set` writes `settings.toml`; a running server reads the change within about a second and the web UI refreshes. The server's address and port take effect the next time it starts.","locale":"en"},"11203":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-79","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"**Jobs**: the command line's jobs are in the database too, so `mizuoto job list` shows the server's jobs and the web UI's **Jobs** panel shows the command line's. Each job records the process that runs it; a process opening the data folder marks unfinished jobs **Interrupted** only when their process has ended, never those of another process still running.","locale":"en"},"11204":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-80","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"**No shared GPU queue**: a command-line job runs at once in its own process, outside the server's GPU queue, and loads its own copy of the model. If the server has the same model loaded on the same GPU, it is in GPU memory twice; when memory runs short, the job fails with `compute_unavailable` (exit code 9).","locale":"en"},"11205":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-81","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"**Loaded models**: `mizuoto runtime` lists the models the running server holds (it finds the server through `server.json` in the data folder) and `mizuoto runtime --unload [MODEL]` unloads them there.","locale":"en"},"11206":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-82","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"**Cancelling**: `mizuoto job cancel` reaches only jobs of its own process and reports `Job … is not running` for a job the server runs. Cancel those with **Cancel** in the web UI's **Jobs** panel, or `POST /api/v1/jobs/{job_id}/cancel`.","locale":"en"},"11207":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-83","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#using-it-while-a-server-runs","content":"`mizuoto job retry` runs a failed, cancelled or interrupted job again in the foreground (its stored request is planned again).","locale":"en"},"11208":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-84","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#check-the-engines-download-a-model-speak","content":"Without `-m`, `tts.default_model` is used. `mizuoto model spec <model>` lists the voice modes, languages, common parameters and engine options a model takes.","locale":"en"},"11209":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-85","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#clone-and-design-voices","content":"`-v` takes a voice's id or slug (the first column of `mizuoto voice list`).","locale":"en"},"11210":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-86","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#hear-it-as-it-is-made","content":"`--stream` writes a WAV to stdout as the model makes it, for a player:","locale":"en"},"11211":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-87","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#hear-it-as-it-is-made","content":"`--stream` refuses to write to a terminal; the whole result is still kept, and its path goes to stderr.","locale":"en"},"11212":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-88","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#batches-and-parameters","content":"`-p` sets common parameters (`temperature`, `top_p`, `top_k`, `repetition_penalty`, `max_new_tokens`, `num_steps`, `guidance_scale`, `speed`, `duration`, `seed`, `text_normalization`, `segment_silence_ms`), `-O` the engine's own options; values are parsed as JSON. A parameter the model does not take is dropped with a warning by default, or refused (exit code 4) with `--strict`; the default comes from `tts.strict_params`.","locale":"en"},"11213":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-89","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#training","content":"Every trainer runs in Mizuoto's own environment; each stage runs as a child process of the same Python.","locale":"en"},"11214":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-90","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-completion","content":"Open a new terminal afterwards to complete commands, subcommands and options.","locale":"en"},"11215":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-91","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#next","content":"Command reference: every command's arguments and options.","locale":"en"},"11216":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-92","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#next","content":"Configuration and environment variables: settings, environment variables and the data folder.","locale":"en"},"11217":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-93","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#next","content":"FAQ","locale":"en"},"11218":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"page","content":"Acceleration","breadcrumbs":["Mizuoto Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","locale":"en"},"11219":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-0","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","content":"Speed without changing results: the attention dispatcher (sites, references, policies, backends, structured masks, probes), compute.fast, compute.compile, CUDA graphs for decoding steps, sync-free sampling, and the CPU's allocator and thread placement; which opt-in features are not bit-identical.","locale":"en"},"11220":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-1","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"What changes results","locale":"en"},"11221":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-2","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#attention","content":"Attention","locale":"en"},"11222":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-3","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#sites-and-their-references","content":"Sites and their references","locale":"en"},"11223":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-4","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#policies","content":"Policies","locale":"en"},"11224":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-5","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#backends-and-the-chain","content":"Backend