evelopment-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","content":"Every engine gives its upstream's output sample for sample on the CPU (see Engines in depth), and speed work keeps it that way: **a default never changes a result**. Faster paths that compute the same kernels with the same arguments (CUDA graphs, fewer waits for the device, CPU memory and thread placement) are on by default. Faster paths that change the arithmetic (other attention kernels, TF32, `torch.compile`, fused projections) are opt-in, and every output lists the ones that ran. Measurements are in Performance record; GPU memory is in Memory.","locale":"en"},"11234":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-15","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"Feature","locale":"en"},"11235":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-16","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"Setting (default)","locale":"en"},"11236":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-17","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"Results","locale":"en"},"11237":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-18","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"CUDA graphs for decoding steps","locale":"en"},"11238":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-19","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-changes-results","content":"`compute.cuda_graphs` (on)","locale":"en"},"11239":{"id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration-20","page_id":"/en/docs/development-acceleration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-acceleration#what-ch