ance-568","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"The code and settings proven only on the CPU, checked on the free GPUs of the GPU baseline (2026-10-18).","locale":"en"},"13231":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-569","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"**Every change since before round 1, step by step.** The G0 set ran with the code of each step on one GPU (frozen worktrees, each with its own harness), and each step's audio was compared with the step before:","locale":"en"},"13232":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-570","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"From → to","locale":"en"},"13233":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-571","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"Identical on the GPU","locale":"en"},"13234":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-572","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"before round 1 → round 1 (`8a021de`)","locale":"en"},"13235":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-573","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"every engine but VoxCPM (its attention span: below)","locale":"en"},"13236":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-574","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"round 1 → round 2 (`60776a4`)","locale":"en"},"13237":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-575","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"every engine but Fish Speech (its in-place Snake: below)","locale":"en"},"13238":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-576","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"round 2 → the attention dispatcher (`7600f61`)","locale":"en"},"13239":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-577","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"all","locale":"en"},"13240":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-578","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"→ the memory fixes (`d65c482`)","locale":"en"},"13241":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-579","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"all","locale":"en"},"13242":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-580","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"→ CUDA graphs for every engine (`0b70d0f`)","locale":"en"},"13243":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-581","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"all (CosyVoice failed on `cuda:1`: below)","locale":"en"},"13244":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-582","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"→ 0.2.5 (`4e6fe35`)","locale":"en"},"13245":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-583","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"all; and on `cuda:1` identical to G0's `cuda:0`","locale":"en"},"13246":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-584","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"Fixed, so the GPU's audio is again the code before's:","locale":"en"},"13247":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-585","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"**VoxCPM's attention span.** On CUDA a step takes SDPA's math path, whose matrix-vector product and softmax split their sums by the key length: a cut at the next multiple of 256 (or 512 … 4096) differs from the whole 8192-position cache at most positions in bf16, fp16 and fp32. The span is now used on the CPU only (`minicpm.attend_span`); on a GPU a step attends over the whole cache, as upstream. Identical to the code before round 1 again, at a cost: warm requests 1.24 → 2.13 s (VoxCPM 2) and 0.68 → 0.96 s (1.5).","locale":"en"},"13248":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-586","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"**Fish Speech's in-place Snake.** On a GPU the codec runs under bf16 autocast, which computes `pow` and `reciprocal` in float32; upstream's Snake therefore ends in float32 while the in-place form, which keeps its buffer's dtype, stayed in bf16 (up to 0.1 apart). The in-place form now runs only without autocast; identical to round 1 again, at the same speed. The unit test covers autocast. (Later, against upstream itself, it turned out that its TorchScript Snake runs in float32 throughout under autocast. Since mizuoto-fishspeech 0.3.3 the port does too, and the decoded audio on a GPU changed: Fish Speech.)","locale":"en"},"13249":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-587","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"**CosyVoice on `cuda:1`** faulted with an illegal memory access: its decoder-step graphs were captured and replayed while `cuda:0` was current, and a replay runs on the current device's stream. Captured and replayed under `torch.cuda.device(graphs.device)` now, as the other engines do (Acceleration).","locale":"en"},"13250":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-588","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"The rotary tables, IndexTTS's in-place GELU and Fish Speech's Snake give their reference's bits on CUDA in fp32, fp16 and bf16 (the exactness tests now run on CUDA when a GPU is visible); CosyVoice's U-Net mask is the same tensor made once. Fish Speech's GPU training replays upstream's initialisation on the CPU generator, as upstream builds its model on the CPU.","locale":"en"},"13251":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-589","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"**The memory plan's mechanisms on CUDA** (G0's set, each compared with G0's audio): every model loaded partly under `compute.vram_limit_mb` at about half its size, the rest streaming, with prefetch on 2, 1 and 0 side streams; out-of-memory errors injected into every phase, each phase run again with half its weights streamed and its generators put back; `compute.kv_cache = static`. All 56 runs identical.","locale":"en"},"13252":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-590","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"Case (whole: warm s)","locale":"en"},"13253":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-591","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"Partly loaded, 2 side streams","locale":"en"},"13254":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-592","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"1","locale":"en"},"13255":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-593","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"0","locale":"en"},"13256":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-594","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"Qwen3-TTS base-clone-en (1.28)","locale":"en"},"13257":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-595","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"24.6 s, 171 GB streamed","locale":"en"},"13258":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-596","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"20.0 s","locale":"en"},"13259":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-597","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"18.6 s, 156 GB","locale":"en"},"13260":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-598","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"VoxCPM v2-clone-en (1.24)