ent-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"Prefetch helps the models run once per request (F5-TTS, OmniVoice: the slowdown is 0.8× the streamed bytes' transfer time, within the plan's 1.2×) and hurts the autoregressive ones, which also stream more with more side streams: the prefetch buffers come out of the room left for resident weights. Qwen3-TTS's talker: 1.8× the transfer time with 2 streams, 1.3× with none.","locale":"en"},"13278":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-616","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"`compute.kv_cache = static` is identical on CUDA and no faster (Qwen3-TTS 1.28 → 1.30 s, CosyVoice 3 0.95 → 0.95 s), with the same peak: `dynamic` stays the default.","locale":"en"},"13279":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-617","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"**The plan's targets (§9)**, from `scripts/parity/memory.py` (one case per process; it now runs on a GPU: the cap reaches the runtime as `compute.vram_limit_mb`):","locale":"en"},"13280":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-618","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"Case","locale":"en"},"13281":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-619","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"Whole","locale":"en"},"13282":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-620","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"12 GB","locale":"en"},"13283":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-621","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performanc