":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"15.2 s","locale":"en"},"13310":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-648","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"the other eight cases","locale":"en"},"13311":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-649","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"2.5–5.4 s","locale":"en"},"13312":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-650","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"at most +1 s","locale":"en"},"13313":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-651","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"(first request in a fresh process, load included)","locale":"en"},"13314":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-652","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"**Smallest card**: every model runs on a 4 GB card, Fish Speech S2 Pro included (the plan aimed at 8 GB). Once a 6 GB run of Fish Speech under the 0.2.5 code ran out of memory while both GPUs were busy; it did not happen again in two more runs.","locale":"en"},"13315":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-653","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"**Offload with a host copy** takes 0.05–0.12 s, no transfer.","locale":"en"},"13316":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-654","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"**Reload** reaches 5.7–8.3 GB/s, 43–62 % of the pinned bandwidth, short of the plan's 80 %: the host copies are pageable (`pinned_bytes` 0), copied tensor by tensor.","locale":"en"},"13317":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-655","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"**Settings on a GPU run.** `compute.cpu_allocator` and `compute.cpu_threads` change neither the warm time nor the load beyond the noise (two interleaved rounds, four engines). Of the CUDA allocators, `expandable` gives identical audio and weights with a little less memory reserved; `async` crashed every engine with CUDA graphs (illegal memory access after a capture): graphs are now not captured under it (`graphs.usable`), which runs, identical, without their speed (Fish Speech 3.1 → 7.3 s, Qwen3-TTS 1.3 → 2.0 s). Training stages now get the allocator in their environment whether or not the host has loaded a model.","locale":"en"},"13318":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-656","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"**Working memory on long texts** (about 30 s of speech, whole models): every language model stays well within its estimate (2–64 %), but the decoders go over, more as the text grows: VoxCPM 1.5's VAE 810 MB against 290 estimated, VoxCPM 2's 440 against 302, Fish Speech's codec 806 against 486, IndexTTS 1.5's BigVGAN 596 against 369, IndexTTS 2's 421 against 358. The calibration raises an estimate after a phase has measured more, and the out-of-memory retry covers the first time; the estimates are to be raised (done: memory estimates).","locale":"en"},"13319":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-657","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"**Training memory presets** on the GPU, the estimate (`MethodInfo.memory_mb`) against the measured peak, MB:","locale":"en"},"13320":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-658","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"Fine-tune","locale":"en"},"13321":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-659","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"`standard`","locale":"en"},"13322":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-660","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"`low`","locale":"en"},"13323":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-661","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"`lowest`","locale":"en"},"13324":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-662","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"`lowest` identical to `standard`","locale":"en"},"13325":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-663","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"F5-TTS full","locale":"en"},"13326":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-664","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-checks-of-the-cpu-rounds-g1","content":"7,576 / 8,821","locale":"en"},"13327":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-665","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-