,"url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"VoxCPM 2","locale":"en"},"13553":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-891","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"2.6–3.7 → 2.7–2.8","locale":"en"},"13554":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-892","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"4,811 → 1,630","locale":"en"},"13555":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-893","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"5,410 → 4,757","locale":"en"},"13556":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-894","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"5,992 → 6,005","locale":"en"},"13557":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-895","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"Fish S2 Pro","locale":"en"},"13558":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-896","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"10.0–17.2 → 4.4–5.4","locale":"en"},"13559":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-897","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"3,770 → 1,546","locale":"en"},"13560":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-898","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"10,542 → 9,071","locale":"en"},"13561":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-899","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"10,923 → 10,877","locale":"en"},"13562":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-900","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"Warm requests, reloads (0.25–3.6 s) and GPU memory are unchanged. With the default host copies the RAM a model holds is its page-locked host copy either way (page-locking copies the file's pages). The peaks left with host copies off were the casts before loading, which wrote the module's memory before the checkpoint's tensors replaced it (Fish S2 Pro: 9 GB; removed below). A process with nothing loaded holds 0.43 GB.","locale":"en"},"13563":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-901","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"**Casting without copying** (`loading.cast`, the next change): the casts before loading no longer write the model once in RAM. Host copies off, the peak RAM (and the RAM held, now the same) against 0.2.26: Fish S2 Pro 9,071 → 1,507 MB, VoxCPM 2 4,757 → 1,524, Qwen3-TTS 3,952 → 1,637 MB; loads fall again (Fish S2 Pro 4.4–5.4 → 2.1 s with the defaults, 1.4 s with host copies off; VoxCPM 2 2.7 → 1.7 s; Qwen3-TTS 1.9–2.4 → 1.4 s). With the defaults RAM is within 4 % of before. Outputs identical. A first version cast each parameter and buffer itself and skipped modules' own `_apply`: `Rotary`'s `inv_freq`, which its `_apply` keeps float32, was rounded to bfloat16 and Qwen3-TTS's and OmniVoice's audio changed; it now casts through `_apply`, as `Module.to` does (the five engines' tensors, loaded in bfloat16 on the CPU both ways, are identical).","locale":"en"},"13564":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-902","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"Found on the way:","locale":"en"},"13565":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-903","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"**glibc kept the freed memory.** Without `trim_heap` the cast's freed allocations (each under glibc's 32 MB mmap threshold) stayed resident: with host copies kept, Qwen3-TTS held 7.2 GB instead of 5.2, VoxCPM 2 9.0 instead of 6.0. Before this change, with host copies off, the same retention held 2–3 GB.","locale":"en"},"13566":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-904","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"**CPU weights left in the file were slower.** IndexTTS 2 on the CPU, its 64-byte-aligned pickles left in the file, decoded in 48.8–49.1 s against 43.0–43.3 back to back (identical audio); a large matrix product over the same file pages was not slower. Weights the CPU computes with are now always copied.","locale":"en"},"13567":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-905","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"**torch imported before the CPU settings.** A first version imported `runtime/loading.py` (torch) in `LocalEngine.load` before the runtime applied `compute.cpu_allocator` and thread placement: every CPU operator ran 40 % slower (F5-TTS 42.8 → 60 s, attention included). A test now loads a model in a fresh process and checks the order.","locale":"en"},"13568":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-906","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#loading-without-a-ram-copy-g10","content":"**Alignment.** float32 `F.linear` on one row gives other last bits for a weight 8 bytes off a 16-byte boundary on this CPU (bf16, fp16 and two rows or more: identical at every offset).","locale":"en"},"13569":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-907","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"2026-11-04, RTX 3060 (torch 2.8 + CUDA 12.8), G1's long cases (about 30 s of speech), warm requests (two per process), two rounds each way, alternated. `QwenDecoder.fuse` (each layer's q/k/v and gate/up as one product, as Qwen3-TTS's `fused_projections`) on the language model:","locale":"en"},"13570":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-908","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"Model","locale":"en"},"13571":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-909","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"Exact","locale":"en"},"13572":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-910","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"Fused","locale":"en"},"13573":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-911","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"Audio","locale":"en"},"13574":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-912","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"CosyVoice 2, fp32 (default)","locale":"en"},"13575":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-913","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"10.42–10.45 s","locale":"en"},"13576":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-914","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"10.31–10.32 s (−1.1 %)","locale":"en"},"13577":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-915","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"identical","locale":"en"},"13578":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-916","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"CosyVoice 3, fp32","locale":"en"},"13579":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-917","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"12.17–12.19 s","locale":"en"},"13580":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-918","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"12.04–12.06 s (−1.1 %)","locale":"en"},"13581":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-919","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"identical","locale":"en"},"13582":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-920","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"CosyVoice 2,