d-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"OmniVoice (bf16)","locale":"en"},"13591":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-929","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"6.59–6.63 s","locale":"en"},"13592":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-930","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"6.63–6.67 s (+0.6 %)","locale":"en"},"13593":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-931","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"different","locale":"en"},"13594":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-932","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#fused-projections-for-cosyvoice-and-omnivoice-g11","content":"CosyVoice 2 and 3 offer it (`engines.cosyvoice.load_options.fused_projections`, off; identical on the CPU for both parity cases). OmniVoice's decoder runs over the whole sequence at every step, products large enough that fusing three into one saves nothing: not offered. Under `fp16` CosyVoice 2 was slower than in fp32 (19.8 against 10.4 s), and in each process the first request's audio differed from the next ones': found and fixed in G12, below. (With `fp16` the fused audio is longer or shorter, so those rows compare time per second of audio.)","locale":"en"},"13595":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-933","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#cosyvoices-fp16-g12","content":"2026-11-04, the same RTX 3060 and long cases. Under `fp16` each token of the language model ran in its own autocast region (the engine runs only inside `next()`), and autocast keeps its float16 casts of the weights only for a region: every token cast all of the language model's weights again (47,416 copies in one short request, 0.5 s of the device's time). Upstream holds one region over the whole generation. With CUDA graphs it also changed the audio: the first request's differed from the later ones', and both from the eager path's (upstream's order of work). The language model's linear layers now hold their weights in float16 under `fp16` (the values autocast casts them to; embeddings and norms stay float32):","locale":"en"},"13596":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-934","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#cosyvoices-fp16-g12","content":"Before (per request)","locale":"en"},"13597":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-935","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#cosyvoices-fp16-g12","content":"After (per request, ms per second of audio)","locale":"en"},"13598":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-936","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#cosyvoices-fp16-g12","content":"fp32, for comparison","locale":"en"},"13599":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-937","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#cosyvoices-fp16-g12","content":"CosyVoice 2, \\~30 s","locale":"en"},"13600":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-938","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#cosyvoices-fp16-g12","content":"19.8 s","locale":"en"},"13601":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-939","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#cosyvoices-fp16-g12","content":"6.2 s (204)","locale":"en"},"13602":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-940","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#cosyvoices-fp16-g12","content":"10.4 s (345)","locale":"en"},"13603":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-941","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#cosyvoices-fp16-g12","content":"CosyVoice 3, \\~31 s","locale":"en"},"13604":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-942","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#cosyvoices-fp16-g12","content":"15.5 s","locale":"en"},"13605":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-943","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#cosyvoices-fp16-g12","content":"6.1 s (198)","locale":"en"},"13606":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-944","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#cosyvoices-fp16-g12","content":"12.2 s (361)","locale":"en"},"13607":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-945","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#cosyvoices-fp16-g12","content":"Audio (three requests per process, each hashed): before, eager gave one audio every request and graphs gave another for the first request and a third after; now eager and graphs give the eager audio every request, for both models, which is what the code before gave eagerly.","locale":"en"},"13608":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-946","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"2026-11-04, RTX 3060 12 GB, the defaults (bf16 or fp16 on the GPU, CUDA graphs, host copies), one model per process, its short parity case and G1's long one (about 30 s of speech), two requests each. Every model loaded whole. \"Process\" is the GPU memory nvidia-smi gave the process at its most (the CUDA context and the allocator's cache included); \"torch\" the most torch held (the new `meta.memory.peak_mb`). The catalogue's `vram_mb`, which the web UI shows as the GPU memory a model takes and the doctor's `fits` weighs, was set from estimates and now is the torch figure rounded up (the reserve, `compute.vram_reserve_mb`, covers the rest):","locale":"en"},"13609":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-947","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"Model (the more of the two cases)","locale":"en"},"13610":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-948","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"Process MB","locale":"en"},"13611":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-949","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"Torch MB","locale":"en"},"13612":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-950","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"`vram_mb`","locale":"en"},"13613":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-951","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"Fish S2 Pro","locale":"en"},"13614":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-952","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"11,873","locale":"en"},"13615":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-953","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#gpu-memory-per-model-g13","content":"10,