erformance-1330","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#experts-kept-in-files-2026-11-05","content":"+0.6 %","locale":"en"},"13993":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1331","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#experts-kept-in-files-2026-11-05","content":"Fish S2 Pro","locale":"en"},"13994":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1332","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#experts-kept-in-files-2026-11-05","content":"`vram_limit_mb=4096`","locale":"en"},"13995":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1333","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#experts-kept-in-files-2026-11-05","content":"228.3 / 228.3","locale":"en"},"13996":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1334","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#experts-kept-in-files-2026-11-05","content":"229.5 / 228.8","locale":"en"},"13997":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1335","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#experts-kept-in-files-2026-11-05","content":"+0.4 %","locale":"en"},"13998":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1336","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#experts-kept-in-files-2026-11-05","content":"Every run's audio was identical to 0.2.36's first round (39 comparisons). The differences are within the runs' own spread; none of these models has a file-backed weight, so the only new work on their path is a check of each host tensor's storage when it is pinned. This build had neither the per-row cancel check nor the full-disk guard, added after: the first runs only for row-streamed layers (Drama 3's alone), the second only when a file is made, so neither is on these engines' path; Drama 3 was timed again with the final code (below).","locale":"en"},"13999":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1337","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#experts-kept-in-files-2026-11-05","content":"On the CPU (the 13 cases of the CPU rounds, a Ryzen 9 5900X shared with another workload, the same two builds alternated, two rounds each): all 39 comparisons identical; the warm runs differ by −7.2 to +5.0 % in both directions, −0.4 % on average, within that machine's spread (the base build's own two rounds differ by up to 12 %). On the CPU nothing streams, so nothing new runs there but the storage check in `host_bytes`.","locale":"en"},"14000":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1338","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#experts-kept-in-files-2026-11-05","content":"Drama 3 itself, which could not load on this machine before (its 30 GiB of experts beside the rest of the model in 31 GB), with the final code: 21.5 GB of experts in files, 16.3 GB in page-locked RAM, 9.1 GB on the GPU; the first load 81 s; a warm request of 5.5–8.3 s of speech 129–162 s, 176–226 GB copied to the GPU a request (1.4 GB/s; the link carries 2.9); each case's two runs identical; RAM never under 7.9 GB available. Read from the disk in a warm request (`/proc/self/io`): 32.4, 27.8, 15.2 and 17.1 GiB (clone en, clone zh, its own voice with tags, dialogue). With 57 % of the experts in files, about 100–130 GB of a request's reads come from them, so the page cache served 72–87 % of those and the disk 13–28 % (8–15 % of all that was copied). Its contract suite with a reference clip: load, every voice mode in English and Chinese (Whisper's WER under 0.35), seeds and segments, streaming, unloading and no residue pass. Cancelling took 2.0 s against the suite's 2 s, from a cancel that arrived while the backbone was being placed again after the unloading test: copying 9 GB to the GPU and page-locking 17 GB of RAM (44 s on its first placement) check for no cancel; cancelled while generating, it stopped within 0.1 s.","locale":"en"},"14001":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1339","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#not-done-because-it-changes-results","content":"bf16 or quantised weights, another thread count, the tanh form of GELU, SDPA's grouped-query path for Fish Speech's repeated heads, a static KV cache by default.","locale":"en"},"14002":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1340","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#not-done-because-it-changes-results","content":"Truncating VoxCPM's attention to exactly the filled positions: identical in bf16, not in fp32 (the kernel's blocks change); the cut at a multiple of 256 is identical in both.","locale":"en"},"14003":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1341","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#not-done-because-it-changes-results","content":"`foreach=True` Adam/AdamW: identical for float32 parameters but slower on the CPU (1032 against 748 ms a step for 100 tensors of 2048 × 2048; Qwen3-TTS's training ×0.92). `fused=True` AdamW: its results differ.","locale":"en"},"14004":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1342","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#not-done-because-it-changes-results","content":"Caching weight norm within a step for GPT-SoVITS's discriminators: the gradients would sum in another order.","locale":"en"},"14005":{"id":"/en/docs/development-performance-1343","page_id":"/en/docs/development-performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-performance#not-done-because-it-changes-results","content":"For Qwen3-TTS on CUDA: a static cache bucketed by 256 with a mask (another SDPA kernel), and batching a long text's segments (other draws).","locale":"en"},"14006":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"page","content":"Release","breadcrumbs":["Mizuoto Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release","locale":"en"},"14007":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-0","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release","content":"Mizuoto's dependencies and why, the platforms it supports, and how its distributions are made and checked: versions released on their own, wheels, the smoke test, CI and the release workflow, the Docker image, the model mirror and this docs site.","locale":"en"},"14008":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-1","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release#dependencies","content":"Dependencies","locale":"en"},"14009":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-2","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Required","locale":"en"},"14010":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-3","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"Optional extras","locale":"en"},"14011":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-4","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release#no-longer-needed","content":"No longer needed","locale":"en"},"14012":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-5","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release#torch-and-platforms","content":"torch and platforms","locale":"en"},"14013":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-6","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release#versions","content":"Versions","locale":"en"},"14014":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-7","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release#wheels-scriptsbuild_wheelspy","content":"Wheels: `scripts/build_wheels.py`","locale":"en"},"14015":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-8","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release#smoke-test-scriptssmoke_wheelspy","content":"Smoke test: `scripts/smoke_wheels.py`","locale":"en"},"14016":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-9","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release#ci-and-the-release-workflow","content":"CI and the release workflow","locale":"en"},"14017":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-10","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release#docker","content":"Docker","locale":"en"},"14018":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-11","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release#the-model-mirror-scriptsmirror_modelspy","content":"The model mirror: `scripts/mirror_models.py`","locale":"en"},"14019":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-12","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release#the-docs-site","content":"The docs site","locale":"en"},"14020":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-13","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release","content":"A release produces three distributions: `mizuoto` (wheel and sdist, with the built web UI inside, every engine under a permissive licence included) and the wheels of the two licence-gated engines, `mizuoto-fishspeech` and `mizuoto-indextts`. All three install into one environment over a torch the user chose, and each is versioned, checked and released on its own. This page covers how they are built, checked and published to PyPI (with twine, by the release workflow).","locale":"en"},"14021":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-14","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#dependencies","content":"Mizuoto is one environment: the dependencies of the core, the API, the command line, the web UI and every engine are in `pyproject.toml` and install at once. Every new dependency must answer three questions: does it have wheels for every platform CI covers (Linux x86_64, Windows x86_64, macOS arm64, CPython 3.10–3.14), does it change results, does it change process-wide state.","locale":"en"},"14022":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-15","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"For","locale":"en"},"14023":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-16","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Packages","locale":"en"},"14024":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-17","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Notes","locale":"en"},"14025":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-18","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Web and command line","locale":"en"},"14026":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-19","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"fastapi (≥ 0.115.3), starlette (≥ 0.40), uvicorn, websockets, python-socketio, pydantic 2, httpx, typer (\\< 0.28), rich, tomli-w, tomli (Python \\< 3.11), send2trash","locale":"en"},"14027":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-20","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Starlette 0.40's `FileResponse` honours Range, so the player seeks; uvicorn speaks WebSocket only with websockets installed; typer has an upper bound because the command line uses its private modules","locale":"en"},"14028":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-21","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Audio","locale":"en"},"14029":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-22","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"av (PyAV), numpy","locale":"en"},"14030":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-23","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Decoding, encoding and resampling through PyAV, the rest with numpy; no ffmpeg or sox program is called","locale":"en"},"14031":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-24","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Runtime","locale":"en"},"14032":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-25","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"torch (≥ 2.8), safetensors, soxr, tokenizers","locale":"en"},"14033":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-26","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"torch's build is the user's (below); soxr is the resampler librosa calls; tokenizers builds the BPE transformers builds","locale":"en"},"14034":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-27","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Text","locale":"en"},"14035":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-28","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"pypinyin, rjieba, jieba, opencc, kaldifst, inflect, tiktoken, regex, wordsegment, budoux, ToJyutping, fasttext-predict (fasttext-predict-v2 on Python 3.14: the same sources, released with 3.14 wheels), pyyaml","locale":"en"},"14036":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-29","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"Many versions are **pinned** (`pypinyin==0.55.0`, `opencc==1.4.2`, `inflect==7.3.1`…): the engines' output depends on them, and another version changes phones and audio","locale":"en"},"14037":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-30","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#required","content":"The licence-gated packages bring a few of their own: `mizuoto-fishspeech` needs tokenizers and safetensors, `mizuoto-indextts` sentencepiece. Each also names the packages it imports directly that Mizuoto already brings (torch and numpy; `mizuoto-indextts` also pyyaml and tiktoken), with Mizuoto's bounds, so its dependencies do not rest on Mizuoto's.","locale":"en"},"14038":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-31","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"Extra","locale":"en"},"14039":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-32","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"Packages","locale":"en"},"14040":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-33","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"For","locale":"en"},"14041":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-34","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release#optional-extras","content":"`mizuoto[gptsovits-ja]`","locale":"en"},"14042":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-35","page_id":"/en/d