docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"Installing reaches PyPI and the PyTorch download site; downloading models reaches Hugging Face, hf-mirror or ModelScope (chosen in **Settings › Downloads**)","locale":"en"},"16923":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-24","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#requirements","content":"No system programs are needed: audio decoding, resampling and the text front ends ship in Python wheels.","locale":"en"},"16924":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-25","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"Mizuoto is on PyPI as `mizuoto`; the licence-gated engines are `mizuoto-fishspeech` and `mizuoto-indextts`. Use a virtual environment of your choice. Install torch first, from the index that matches your machine, so that installing Mizuoto keeps that build:","locale":"en"},"16925":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-26","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"Then Mizuoto, in one install; add the gated engines when you want them:","locale":"en"},"16926":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-27","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"uv works the same way: `uv pip install mizuoto` in a virtual environment.","locale":"en"},"16927":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-28","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"You need uv, and bun to build the web UI.","locale":"en"},"16928":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-29","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"The full development setup is in Development setup.","locale":"en"},"16929":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-30","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"One image holds the server, the UI and every engine, with GPT-SoVITS's Japanese and Korean front ends; models go to the `/data` volume.","locale":"en"},"16930":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-31","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"Build argument","locale":"en"},"16931":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-32","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"16932":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-33","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"16933":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-34","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"`TORCH_INDEX`","locale":"en"},"16934":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-35","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"`https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128`","locale":"en"},"16935":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-36","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"The torch build: another CUDA (`cu126`…`cu132`), ROCm (`rocm6.4`…`rocm7.2`) or `cpu` index","locale":"en"},"16936":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-37","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"`TORCH`","locale":"en"},"16937":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-38","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"`torch>=2.8`","locale":"en"},"16938":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-39","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"The torch requirement, such as `torch==2.8.0`","locale":"en"},"16939":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-40","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"`GATED`","locale":"en"},"16940":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-41","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"`0`","locale":"en"},"16941":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-42","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"`1` adds Fish Speech and IndexTTS; their licences must still be accepted in the UI or on the command line","locale":"en"},"16942":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-43","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"`PYTHON`","locale":"en"},"16943":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-44","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"`3.11`","locale":"en"},"16944":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-45","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"The image's Python","locale":"en"},"16945":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-46","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"In the container the server listens on `0.0.0.0`, so set an access token with `MIZUOTO_SERVER__ACCESS_TOKEN`. The browser shows an **Access token** dialog when the page opens; enter it there.","locale":"en"},"16946":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-47","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"The image has a health check (`/api/v1/app/health`).","locale":"en"},"16947":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-48","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#ways-to-install","content":"More in Docker.","locale":"en"},"16948":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-49","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#optional-extras","content":"Some languages need packages that are not installed by default. Without them, text in those languages fails with the install command in the error's hint; `mizuoto doctor` lists the missing ones.","locale":"en"},"16949":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-50","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#optional-extras","content":"Extra","locale":"en"},"16950":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-51","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#optional-extras","content":"For","locale":"en"},"16951":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-52","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#optional-extras","content":"Note","locale":"en"},"16952":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-53","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#optional-extras","content":"`pip install 'mizuoto[gptsovits-ja]'`","locale":"en"},"16953":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-54","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#optional-extras","content":"GPT-SoVITS's Japanese","locale":"en"},"16954":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-55","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#optional-extras","content":"pyopenjtalk 0.4.1 is published as source only: building it needs CMake and a C++ compiler","locale":"en"},"16955":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-56","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#optional-extras","content":"`pip install 'mizuoto[gptsovits-ko]'`","locale":"en"},"16956":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-57","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#optional-extras","content":"GPT-SoVITS's Korean","locale":"en"},"16957":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-58","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#optional-extras","content":"python-mecab-ko and jamo; python-mecab-ko 1.3.7 publishes wheels for Python 3.10–3.12 only, so on 3.13 and 3.14 it is built from source and needs mecab-ko installed (`mecab-config`)","locale":"en"},"16958":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-59","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#optional-extras","content":"`pip install 'mizuoto-indextts[ja]'`","locale":"en"},"16959":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-60","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#optional-extras","content":"IndexTTS-2.5's Japanese","locale":"en"},"16960":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-61","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#optional-extras","content":"fugashi and unidic-lite","locale":"en"},"16961":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-62","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#checking-the-installation","content":"`mizuoto doctor` lists the GPUs it finds (with `nvidia-smi`, `rocm-smi` or `amd-smi`, or by asking torch; see Performance), reports the torch build against them (with the exact install command when they do not match), whether each engine is available or what it still needs (torch, or a licence-gated engine's distribution), and the optional extras that are missing. In the web UI, **Settings › Compute** shows the torch check, and **Check this machine** on each engine card under **Models › Engines** shows that engine's.","locale":"en"},"16962":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-63","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#starting","content":"Useful options:","locale":"en"},"16963":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-64","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#starting","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"16964":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-65","page_id":"