,"`torch.compile` on the CPU"],[10900,"`torch.compile` the heavy modules of F5-TTS, CosyVoice, GPT-SoVITS v4/v5 and IndexTTS, and Fish Speech S2 Pro's decoding steps; VoxCPM is slower with it on a GPU (no CUDA graphs); applies to models loaded after the change (see Performance)"],[2704,"`torch.compile`（`compute.compile`）"],[6228,"`torch`"],[14752,"`torch`"],[351,"`TORCH`"],[5618,"`TORCH`"],[8413,"`TORCH`"],[8875,"`TORCH`"],[14142,"`TORCH`"],[16936,"`TORCH`"],[9679,"`torch`: install the build `mizuoto doctor` names (see Installation)."],[1155,"`torch`：安装 `mizuoto doctor` 指出的构建（见安装）。"],[352,"`torch>=2.8`"],[5619,"`torch>=2.8`"],[8414,"`torch>=2.8`"],[8876,"`torch>=2.8`"],[14143,"`torch>=2.8`"],[16937,"`torch>=2.8`"],[2039,"`train delete {experiment}`"],[10563,"`train delete {experiment}`"],[2033,"`train edit {experiment}`"],[10557,"`train edit {experiment}`"],[2036,"`train export {experiment}`"],[10560,"`train export {experiment}`"],[2018,"`train list`"],[10542,"`train list`"],[2012,"`train methods {model}`"],[10536,"`train methods {model}`"],[2030,"`train metrics {experiment}`"],[10554,"`train metrics {experiment}`"],[2015,"`train new {name}`"],[10539,"`train new {name}`"],[2024,"`train plan {experiment}`"],[10548,"`train plan {experiment}`"],[2027,"`train run {experiment}`"],[10551,"`train run {experiment}`"],[2021,"`train status {experiment}`"],[10545,"`train status {experiment}`"],[266,"`train_metrics`"],[8790,"`train_metrics`"],[5962,"`train.py compare <engine> <name>`"],[14486,"`train.py compare <engine> <name>`"],[5960,"`train.py run <engine> --impl reference\\|native --model <id> --method <m> --hp k=v --name <n>`"],[14484,"`train.py run <engine> --impl reference\\|native --model <id> --method <m> --hp k=v --name <n>`"],[3900,"`train.py`"],[6737,"`train.py`"],[7098,"`train.py`"],[12424,"`train.py`"],[15261,"`train.py`"],[15622,"`train.py`"],[15316,"`train.py`, `finetune.py`"],[15189,"`train.py`, `sft.py`"],[15693,"`train.py`, `sft.py`"],[15774,"`train.py`, `sft.py`"],[15459,"`train.py`, `train_s1.py`, `train_s2.py`, `s2_modules.py`, `s2_lora.py`"],[6792,"`train.py`、`finetune.py`"],[6665,"`train.py`、`sft.py`"],[7169,"`train.py`、`sft.py`"],[7250,"`train.py`、`sft.py`"],[6935,"`train.py`、`train_s1.py`、`train_s2.py`、`s2_modules.py`、`s2_lora.py`"],[1567,"`train`"],[10091,"`train`"],[14889,"`train`: upstream's fine-tune loop with its SDPA configs: the shards read by data-loader workers seeded as upstream seeds them, length-grouped batches under a 4-D mask, the masked cross-entropy, AdamW with the cosine schedule, gradient clipping and accumulation. LoRA is peft's, written without peft. Each update's loss is a `ctx.metric`. It ends with `out/checkpoint-<steps>` in upstream's layout."],[6365,"`train`：上游的微调循环及其 SDPA 配置：分片由数据加载 worker 读取，worker 的播种方式与上游相同；按长度分组成批，使用四维掩码；带掩码的交叉熵、带余弦调度的 AdamW、梯度裁剪和梯度累积。LoRA 就是 peft 的那种，但不依赖 peft 实现。每次更新的损失记为一次 `ctx.metric`。最后以上游的目录结构写出 `out/checkpoint-<步数>`。"],[3834,"`TRAINER`"],[12358,"`TRAINER`"],[2533,"`training.attention`"],[2791,"`training.attention`"],[11057,"`training.attention`"],[11315,"`training.attention`"],[2545,"`training.deterministic`"],[11069,"`training.deterministic`"],[2521,"`training.devices`"],[11045,"`training.devices`"],[2537,"`training.keep_checkpoints`"],[11061,"`training.keep_checkpoints`"],[2529,"`training.memory`"],[11053,"`training.memory`"],[15216,"`training.memory`: gradient checkpointing over the language model's or the flow's blocks gives identical losses and weights."],[15803,"`training.memory`: gradient checkpointing over the MiniCPM layers, the local encoder's and the DiT's gives identical results (LoRA dropout and CFM draws replayed); the VAE's decoder stays off the device; for LoRA, `low` stores the frozen linear weights in the autocast dtype (CUDA) and `lowest` streams them from RAM (identical on the CPU)."],[15644,"`training.memory`: gradient checkpointing over the Qwen3 layers (LoRA's dropout masks replayed); for LoRA, `low` also stores the frozen linear weights in the autocast dtype (CUDA: autocast casts them to it at every product anyway) and `lowest` keeps the LoRA layers' frozen base weights in RAM, copied to the GPU for each product, and AdamW's state in RAM. Identical on the CPU (the tiny trainer's losses and adapter); on a GPU with deterministic kernels, the same loss and gradients with float32 and bfloat16 frozen weights. The LoRA's peak: 7.3 GB, 2.1 GB under `low`, 1.1 GB under `lowest` (RTX 3060, 2026-11-04)."],[15721,"`training.memory`: gradient checkpointing over the talker's and code predictor's layers gives identical results; `lowest` keeps AdamW's state in RAM (float32 there)."],[15279,"`training.memory`: gradient checkpointing over the transformer's blocks gives identical results; `low` keeps the EMA copy in RAM; `lowest` also AdamW's state (identical on the CPU)."],[15485,"`training.memory`: the speech stage frees HuBERT before the speaker model; the semantic stage puts only SoVITS's SSL projection and quantiser on the device."],[15343,"`training.memory`: upstream's per-layer checkpointing stays as it is; under `bf16-true` the LoRA layers keep the checkpoint's own bfloat16 tensors as their frozen weights (memory-mapped from the safetensors files, no copy: the same values), and the export's key order is read from a model built on the meta device. Measured on S2 Pro (2026-10-19, an RTX 3090): the training stage's process holds 0.4 GB of its own memory while loading (8.9 GB with bfloat16 copies, 17 GB with float32 ones) and peaks at 5 GB resident; the export holds the merged weights, 9 GB, beside the mapped checkpoint (page cache). Under `lowest` the LoRA linear layers' frozen weights stay in page-locked RAM and are copied to the GPU for each product (`streamed_linear`, the model placed without them): identical (the tiny trainer's losses and LoRA weights on the CPU); S2 Pro's LoRA at batch 2 then peaks at 7.9 GB instead of 15.6 (an RTX 3060, 15.6 s a step there over its PCIe x4 link), and the default batch 4 