e optional fallback (Memory)"],[12576,"A phase under `ctx.use` (one that yields audio or consumes a generator) is not retried, so its estimate must bound what it can reach."],[12626,"A phase's estimate decides whether its weights fit whole, so it is sized by the request (its text tokens, batch rows, the reference's length), not by the worst case `max_new_tokens` allows. Setting aside memory the request never uses pushes weights out for nothing: a worst case of 8192 frames, doubled, was 2.4 GB for a Qwen3-TTS sentence that uses about 20 MB."],[12032,"A plain function in `mizuoto/cli/commands/` with `--json`, registered in `get_app()` of `cli/app.py` (name and help at registration), and added to `EXPECTED_TREE` in `tests/cli/test_cli.py`. See Adding a command"],[16625,"a play button and its length;"],[16160,"a play button for the line's take in use;"],[10677,"A port in use makes it try the next ones (up to 20); when all fail it exits with code 3, and with code 4 when a certificate file does not exist. Binding to an address other than loopback logs a warning that other machines can reach the server. Once started, it prints `SERVER_READY url=http://...` on standard output."],[10130,"A preset speaker of the model"],[10465,"A project is a book, script or dialogue read line by line by a cast of voices. A script is plain text: `#` starts a chapter, `Name: text` is a line of that speaker, a blank line ends a paragraph."],[16114,"A project is saved in `projects/<name>/project.json` in the data folder."],[12254,"A project's lines render as ordinary speak jobs; takes are outputs of kind `line`, stale by request fingerprint"],[16153,"A project's page has three tabs: **Script**, **Cast** and **Export**. The top shows its name, the save state (**Saving…**, **Saved**, **Unsaved changes**) and rendered lines out of all, with their length."],[11886,"A project's render (which submits ordinary speak jobs)"],[15392,"A random model with the real one's shapes but 8 experts did run, on an RTX 3060 (2026-11-03, torch 2.8, bf16, 8.5 GB on the device). Every token still uses 8 experts, so a decoding step does the real model's work."],[12629,"A rare generation that outruns its estimate under `ctx.run` runs again with more weights streamed, exactly."],[14334,"A real engine on your machine"],[10255,"A reference clip (repeatable, required)"],[10981,"A reference clip outside the model's length window: `trim` cuts it at its quietest point before the limit (its transcript no longer matches and is dropped), `reject` refuses it"],[10126,"A reference clip to clone (repeatable)"],[11554,"A refused WebSocket is closed with 1008. socket.io's `connect` handler (`SocketBridge._on_connect`) checks `auth.token` once more."],[14020,"A release produces three distributions: `mizuoto` (wheel and sdist, with the built web UI inside, every engine under a permissive licence included) and the wheels of the two licence-gated engines, `mizuoto-fishspeech` and `mizuoto-indextts`. All three install into one environment over a torch the user chose, and each is versioned, checked and released on its own. This page covers how they are built, checked and published to PyPI (with twine, by the release workflow)."],[12552,"A reload from page-locked copies only queues them: placing S2 Pro's 9 GB returns in 0.9 s, and the copies take 2 s more on an RTX 3060. The request's next wait for the device then waited for all of them without checking for a cancel, so a cancel made right after an unload waited 2.6 s. A phase whose handles gained resident weights on a CUDA device now waits for those copies itself (`manager._await_copies`, an event polled every 5 ms) and checks for a cancel meanwhile. It does so only inside a request, and other phases keep running without a wait. The cancel then takes 0.4 s, and the model stays loaded, its copies finishing on their stream."],[12256,"A remote agent owns its models and engines; requests carry files by content (SHA-256); training stays local"],[8692,"A remote host cannot be reached, refused the token or speaks another protocol"],[11195,"A remote host cannot be reached, refused the token, or speaks another protocol version"],[17013,"A remote host needs the same Mizuoto version as this machine: update both."],[11121,"A remote request whose agent stays silent this long fails (seconds, 10–3600)"],[16746,"a remove button (one clip must remain)."],[16628,"a remove button."],[9885,"A request is batched only when all of these hold:"],[12033,"A route"],[12107,"A route's dependencies are in its signature and tests can pass isolated services; no graph nodes need to share services"],[16649,"A run is one **Train** job whose steps are the stages; its card shows under the stages."],[14850,"A run is one `train` job whose steps are the selected stages:"],[10717,"A running server reads changes to the file within about a second, and open web UIs refresh; saving in the web UI afterwards merges with the file as it is, so it keeps the command line's changes. A broken file makes the server log `Ignored a change to … settings.toml` and keep its settings. `server.host`, `server.port` and the certificates take effect the next time the server starts; changing `engines.<id>.*` unloads that engine's models, which load with the new settings when next used."],[10695,"A sample `settings.toml`"],[14273,"A scratch folder under `<cache>/scratch/<engine>/`, removed when the call ends"],[12045,"A screen"],[14467,"A seeded request gives the same audio before and after another engine's model ran in the process"],[9091,"A server that supports HTTP Range lets interrupted downloads resume."],[12037,"A setting"],[9967,"A short name, used in engine devices (`gpu-box/cuda:0`); not empty, without `/` or `.`"],[12110,"A single user or a small trusted group running it locally; the complexity pays only for multi-tenant serving"],[12397,"A source clip and a voice; a clip, its transcript and `EditSpan`s"],[15397,"A source review against upstream found Mizuoto cutting Drama 3's long text itself (fixed: the variant declares `long_text`) and float16's experts unclamped (fixed), and the request-level differences listed under Deviations."],[8957,"A source that answers 401, 403 or 404 for a file, or serves it with the wrong size or SHA-256, is left for the next one at once. Other errors (a dropped connection, a timeout, a 5xx) are retried on the same source up to 4 times, after 1, 2, 4 and 8 seconds (30 at most). When every source fails, the job ends with `download_failed` (exit code 12); its detail lists the sources tried and the last errors. The job log has one line per file naming the source it came from."],[9277,"a speaker"],[16855,"a speaker"],[16201,"A speaker's settings stay when its model (or the project's) changes, so choosing the first model again brings them back. Each line's request carries only the style instruction, parameters and engine options its model takes; the rest are kept but not used. A kept instruction the model does not follow (or not with this voice) says so under the field, and **Add a style instruction** is not offered for that speaker's lines. A preset speaker or a language the new model lacks is marked on the card: those decide what is said, so the lines fail until you choose again."],[12078,"A Stable Diffusion model manager"],[14864,"A stage method returns a JSON-serialisable dict, stored as the stage's `result`; later stages read it from `ctx.results`. `StageContext` (`mizuoto/training/context.py`) offers:"],[12251,"A stage that logs is evidently alive; a silent one still beats"],[16157,"a state dot (hover for the state's name; see the next section);"],[12105,"A static service locator, `ApiDependencies.invoker`"],[15489,"A streamed middle chunk too short for the SOLA overlap leaves an empty piece, on which upstream's post-processing raises an error; kept as upstream behaves. It has been seen with a `min_chunk_length` of 4."],[12545,"A streamed unit's weights rest in RAM. Forward pre- and post-hooks on the unit, and on each module holding its weights, swap `param.data` to a device copy for the call and back after it. Hooks on the leaves make any path into a layer work (`layer.forward_step(…)`, `vae.decode`), and nothing in `ops` or in a layer's code changes. A component wholly on its device has no hooks at all, so the resident path costs nothing."],[8744,"A synthesis can wait for its result: `POST /api/v1/tts/speak?wait=true&timeout=600` answers with the finished job; `result.output_id` (and `result.output_ids` for a batch) is the result's id. When the job is still running after `timeout` seconds (600 by default, at most 3600) the answer is 504 `timeout` with the job in `detail.job_id`; it goes on, and you read it as usual."],[10265,"A tag (repeatable)"],[9358,"A text in a language whose optional extra is missing fails with `capability_not_supported` and the install command in the hint, for instance `pip install 'mizuoto[gptsovits-ja]'`."],[14858,"A thread emits a `HeartbeatEvent` every 10 s (`HEARTBEAT_SECONDS`)."],[8684,"A time limit passed (for example `wait=true`)"],[14863,"A trainer is a `mizuoto.training.Trainer` subclass with one `stage_<id>(ctx)` method per stage id its methods declare; `ctx.request[\"method\"]` says which method runs. The trainer's module imports no torch at the top: the host imports it to read `REQUIRES` and `DEVICES` (`InferenceService.trainer_needs`) and to ask `refuses(method, model_dir)`, which says, without torch, why a method cannot start from a model (Qwen3-TTS: the 0.6B Base for `speaker`; the method then shows as unavailable, and a run cannot start), so the maths lives in modules it imports inside the stage methods. CosyVoice's trainer, for example, sets `DEVICES = (\"cuda\", \"cpu\")`: upstream trains under torchrun on CUDA only, and nothing in the native port needs CUDA."],[14783,"A training method is `[training.<id>]` in the engine's manifest (`TrainingMethod`). OmniVoice's LoRA:"],[12248,"A training run is one `train` job whose steps are its stages, each stage a child process; the stages are declared statically in the manifest"],[11323,"A training stage binds its policy process-wide (`dispatch.PROCESS_POLICY`), because autograd runs backward passes, and gradient checkpointing's recomputed forwards, on threads of its own."],[8676,"A training stage's process or a remote agent died or stopped answering"],[11186,"A training stage's process or a remote agent died or stopped answering; the engine raised an exception"],[12273,"A tunnel's or proxy's visitors must not browse the server's disk"],[12524,"A unit is a group of weights that moves together: a decoder layer, a DiT block, a vocoder stage (ComfyUI's dynamic-VRAM units)."],[12638,"a unit's weight read outside its `forward` fails (it is not there)."],[12187,"A user's output should not change because the implementation did; where 0.1 differed from upstream on purpose (F5-TTS generating chunks in order rather than on a thread pool), 0.1 is the reference"],[10734,"A value that parses as JSON is used as JSON (numbers, `true`/`false`, lists, objects), else as a string; `null` or `none` means empty."],[12329,"A variant is a set of static capabilities; requests are validated against it before any job exists:"],[16721,"A voice a design model made from a description; the clip it spoke becomes its main clip, so other models can clone it too"],[10182,"A voice attribute `key=value` (repeatable)"],[10280,"A voice attribute `key=value` (repeatable)"],[10134,"A voice attribute `key=value` (repeatable), such as OmniVoice's `gender=female`"],[10178,"A voice design model (required)"],[10276,"A voice design model (required)"],[15675,"A voice from a free-text description"],[16430,"A voice from the voice library"],[8759,"A voice given with the request, in one way only: `references` (`[{\"audio_id\" or \"path\", \"transcript\"}]`), `preset`, `description` / `attributes` (a `consent` field is ignored)"],[11830,"A voice is `voices/<slug>/voice.json` plus `references/<sha256>.flac` (mono, at the clip's own rate). The folders are the truth and the list is a scan; delete goes to the trash. The kinds are `reference`, `designed` (a design result, its clip the primary reference), `preset` (one model's preset speaker) and `trained`."],[14886,"A voice or model exported again is listed once, at its latest export. `mizuoto train export <exp>` runs the `export` stage alone. The exports keep the upstream recipes' formats and weight names, so upstream's implementation (and Mizuoto 0.1) loads them too, and the other way round."],[16725,"A voice with its own fine-tuned weights, from training (see Train)"],[9298,"a voice's weights"],[16870,"a voice's weights"],[12706,"A warm time is the fastest warm run: the machine's other work only ever slows a run down. Comparisons that matter are interleaved, the two codes in separate processes, one after the other."],[8813,"A WAV of unknown length (PCM16 right after the header)"],[12562,"A weight that changes after placement goes through the handle (`handle.replace(module)`: a voice's own GPT-SoVITS weights), so a host copy is never stale."],[11489,"a whole patch per attention span and setting (`PatchDecoder`); the static caches kept with the model"],[15895,"a whole seeded request through Mizuoto's stack"],[16274,"About"],[12997,"About ×7: a token is 40 ms of audio, so the LM went from 1.7× slower than real time to 4× faster. The same tokens for three seeds (about 400 tokens each, to EOS) with and without graphs."],[15345,"About 10 GB of GPU memory to run the model whole (S2 Pro); on a CPU it runs in fp32 and is slow."],[9331,"about 100; Chinese"],[9317,"about 50 (Drama 3: 80+)"],[12570,"Above the manager, `RuntimeService` keeps at most `compute.max_resident_models` models loaded, unloads idle ones after `compute.unload_after_minutes` (server only), moves every idle model off a GPU before a fine-tune there (`release_device`), and after a job fails for running out of memory unloads every model not in use from every GPU (`ComputeService.release_after_oom`, ComfyUI's `unload_all_models`). See Runtime."],[11218,"Acceleration"],[14531,"Acceleration and speed work keep to the same tiers: an acceleration that changes bits (compilation, for one) stays at least within the engine's T1/T3 tolerance, with the measured error recorded; speed work on the default path must not change a bit."],[12260,"Accepting a licence is also required to download the weights and assets; the full text ships with the package and the command line can show it"],[8532,"Access control"],[8697,"Access control has three refusals of its own: `bad_host` (400), `bad_origin` (403) and `auth_required` (401)."],[9646,"Access token"],[10759,"Access token: once set, every API and socket request must carry it"],[10773,"Access tokens, the origin check and the Host check are described in HTTP API."],[16011,"Action"],[16472,"Action"],[11143,"Add `--help` at any level; a group name alone (such as `mizuoto model`) shows that group's help too. Every level accepts `--debug`."],[15002,"Add `keys.projects` to the lists invalidated on reconnect."],[10512,"Add a folder of clips in a known layout"],[10379,"Add a model folder from elsewhere (an earlier download, a fine-tune). When its file sizes match a catalogue model, it is checked by SHA-256 and imported as that model; otherwise it becomes a user model `<engine>/<name>`."],[10293,"Add a model's preset speaker to the library"],[10311,"Add a reference clip"],[10349,"Add a voice from a zip written by `voice export`"],[10249,"Add a voice from reference clips; missing transcripts come from speech recognition."],[8722,"Add a voice's fine-tuned weights from server paths"],[10515,"Add audio files or folders (a `.lab` or `.txt` beside a clip is its text), a voice's references or outputs"],[10479,"Add chapters and lines from a script; new speaker names join the cast"],[11659,"Add it to `EXPECTED_TREE` in `tests/cli/test_cli.py`. `test_command_tree` compares the whole tree, so a