Base image"],[856,"Base（克隆）"],[861,"Base（克隆）"],[11135,"Batches and parameters"],[15560,"Beam sampling used to wait for the device about ten times a step (`torch.multinomial`'s checks, the scorer reading each candidate with `.item()`, the stopping test, the beam reorder, the position embedding's index tensor). Now once: the draw is `multinomial`'s own `topk(p / Exp(1), 2 × beams)` (`runtime.sampling.multinomial_draws`, the same ids and generator state on the CPU and CUDA); the candidates' scores, tokens and beams are read back together and the scorer decides on the host from those values; the position embedding is its table's row. With `compute.cuda_graphs` (NVIDIA, the GPT wholly on its device, with a KV cache: IndexTTS 2/2.5, and 1.5 in fp16) the GPT-2's one-token steps of all beams run as graphs around each layer's attention; the cache, its beam reorder and the sampling stay eager. The same audio, 2.6–3.2 times faster per step on the 1.5's sizes. The beams' keys and values for every layer share one buffer (`BeamCaches`), which a step grows by a position with the beams' rows reordered in one copy per beam, each layer then writing its new key and value in place: each layer's keys and values are the contiguous tensors `index_select` and `torch.cat` made before, at half the copying (×1.11 on 30 s of speech). The graphs are captured per number of beams: until mizuoto-indextts 0.2.6 a one-beam request after a three-beam one replayed the three-beam graphs and failed."],[10977,"Beam search width for transcripts (2–10); 5 is what 0.1 used. More can be slightly more accurate and is slower. Transcripts are cached per width, so a change transcribes a clip again"],[8704,"Bearer header"],[180,"Bearer 头"],[12875,"before"],[12891,"before"],[12935,"before"],[12988,"before"],[13043,"before"],[13000,"Before"],[13014,"Before"],[13596,"Before (per request)"],[12789,"Before → after"],[14305,"Before each phase of a call, idle components on the same device give up memory, unit by unit, to make room; what does not fit streams from RAM (Memory)"],[13234,"before round 1 → round 1 (`8a021de`)"],[9174,"Behaviour"],[15898,"Behaviour is compared along with the audio: the parameters applied and the warnings, the voice mode chosen, the segments, the streamed chunks' lengths, the sample rate and the error codes of invalid requests."],[8975,"Being downloaded"],[16051,"Being downloaded; shows the amount done, the speed and the time left"],[16191,"Being rendered"],[16747,"below it, the clip's transcript; click **Save** (or press Enter) after changing it."],[16309,"Below them are this machine's devices, with each GPU's used and total memory, and the torch in use with its build. When torch is missing or its build does not suit this machine, the problem is shown with the command that installs the right build. Each engine's own device and precision are set under **Models › Engines**; the models loaded now are in the top bar's **Models in memory**."],[9269,"Best at"],[14001,"bf16 or quantised weights, another thread count, the tanh form of GELU, SDPA's grouped-query path for Fish Speech's repeated heads, a static KV cache by default."],[5477,"bf16 或量化权重、其他线程数、GELU 的 tanh 近似、Fish Speech 重复头的 SDPA 分组查询路径、默认使用静态 KV 缓存。"],[12589,"BigVGAN in tiles with context"],[4065,"BigVGAN 带上下文分块解码"],[9327,"bilibili Model Use License (gated)"],[16891,"bilibili Model Use License (licence-gated)"],[803,"bilibili Model Use License（需接受）"],[8368,"bilibili Model Use License（需接受许可）"],[15500,"bilibili's zero-shot TTS (index-tts/index-tts, bilibili Model Use License). The port is under the same licence, so it ships as a distribution of its own, `mizuoto-indextts` (`packages/native/indextts`, package `mizuoto_indextts`, with `LICENSE.txt`), registered under `mizuoto.engines` (`indextts = mizuoto_indextts:IndexTtsEngine`). Downloading and speaking need the licence accepted, and cloning needs a consent statement. On the CPU in fp32 with the same seed IndexTTS-1.5, 2 and 2.5 are identical to Mizuoto 0.1 through the whole stack. User-facing details: Engines in depth."],[9589,"bilibili's zero-shot TTS: clones from a clip without its transcript. Best for: emotion control — IndexTTS-2 takes the emotion from a clip, eight emotion weights or a description; 2.5 adds Japanese, Spanish and speed."],[8623,"Body `{\"model\": \"qwen3tts/1.7b-base\"}` unloads that model (404 when it is not loaded); `{\"model\": null}` unloads every model not in use. Answers the new `RuntimeStatus`"],[11335,"bool, additive"],[11341,"bool, additive"],[14932,"Both kinds read the same tokens and look alike. `@material/web` is in maintenance mode and gains no components; should one break with a future browser or Vue version, it is replaced inside `src/ui/` and feature code does not change."],[15718,"Both losses are transformers' `ForCausalLMLoss`, which shifts the already shifted labels once more; kept."],[15911,"Both were found while comparing E2-TTS: `F.linear` on a strided (non-contiguous) 3-D input takes another CPU kernel, with other rounding, when its weight requires grad, or when the weight is an *inference tensor* (made inside `torch.inference_mode()`), even under `no_grad`. Upstream's weights are ordinary parameters that require grad. So native engines leave parameters as `nn.Module` makes them (no `requires_grad_(False)`), and models are loaded outside inference mode; requests still run inside it."],[13172,"Bound by launches: GPT-SoVITS's GPT (about 56 %) and CosyVoice 2's language model (about 69 %)."],[13171,"Bound by the device's work (about 90 % busy or more): F5-TTS's DiT, IndexTTS's s2mel, BigVGAN and 1.5's GPT, CosyVoice 3's flow, Fish Speech's, Qwen3-TTS 1.7B's, VoxCPM's and OmniVoice's language models. (Capturing OmniVoice's step forward as a CUDA graph, tried in G2, gave 2 %.)"],[8713,"Bound with `--host 0.0.0.0`, the server logs that other machines can reach it, but it does not require a token. The API can delete files, download models and read audio on the server: set an access token, or put the server behind a firewall, a VPN or a reverse proxy with authentication."],[8718,"Browse and register audio files on the server"],[8729,"Browsed and registered paths must also lie inside `paths.browse_roots` (empty: the home folder, the data folder and every drive or volume). Remote clients upload instead: `PUT /audio/files`, or weights role by role with `PUT /voices/{id}/weights/{engine}/{role}`."],[14428,"Browser end-to-end tests (`tests/e2e`, below)"],[14376,"Build `mizuoto` (with the UI) and the gated engines' wheels into `dist/` (`scripts/build_wheels.py`)"],[8845,"Build a Mizuoto image from the repository's Dockerfile: its stages and build arguments, GPUs, volumes, the access token and environment variables, and the command line or an agent in a container."],[14133,"Build argument"],[16930,"Build argument"],[8847,"Build arguments"],[12401,"Build modules from `ops.default` (no random initialisation), load weights with `mizuoto.runtime.loading` (`load_state_dict`, `load_into`, strict), and leave parameters as `nn.Module` makes them. Draw every random number from `ctx.generator_for(device)` or `ctx.rng`, in upstream's order (see Runtime)."],[12365,"Build the model from `spec` (`model_id`, `model_dir`, `variant`, `device`, `dtype`, `options`) and return a `LoadedEngine`; report with `ctx.progress(\"loading:<part>\")`, check `ctx.check_cancel()` between parts"],[14190,"Builds the `Runtime` on first use, from the `compute` settings; says which engines are implemented here, what an engine is missing (`torch`, `mizuoto-fishspeech`…), its extras and its trainer"],[16415,"Button"],[16640,"Button"],[14934,"Button emphasis: at most one filled button per region (a view's main action, such as Speak or Train), tonal for secondary actions, outlined or text for the rest. Interactive elements have a visible focus indicator and, as a rule, a target of at least 48×48px (`dense` controls in compact rows and cards excepted)."],[9243,"By default only local 