l and the flow under CUDA autocast, as upstream's `fp16` does. Upstream holds one autocast region over a whole generation; here each token runs in its own (the engine runs only inside `next()`), and autocast keeps its float16 copies of the weights only for a region, so every token cast all of the language model's weights again: `fp16` ran up to twice as slow as fp32, and with CUDA graphs the first request's audio differed from the later ones' and from the eager path's. The language model's linear layers now hold their weights in float16 under `fp16`, the values autocast computes them with (`_half_linears`, at load; embeddings and norms stay float32, as autocast computes them): the eager path's audio on every request, with or without graphs, 1.7–1.8× faster than fp32 (Performance). Fast mode (load option `fused_projections`, CosyVoice 2 and 3): the Qwen2 language model's q/k/v and gate/up projections as one product each (`QwenDecoder.fuse`, as Qwen3-TTS's), labelled in the output; identical on the CPU, on an RTX 3060 identical in fp32 and 1 % faster per second of audio, 2–5 % faster under `fp16`, where the audio changes."],[9335,"Capability names match the UI, such as **Clone a voice**, **Clone without a transcript**, **Preset speakers**, **Design from a description**, **Design from attributes**, **Its own voice**, **Instructions**, **Streaming**, **Streaming text**, **Batches** and **Long text**. \"Reference clips\" below gives the length window per clip; a clip outside it is refused or cut according to `tts.reference_policy` (see Configuration)."],[11867,"Capacity"],[11474,"Captured"],[12968,"Case"],[13013,"Case"],[13176,"Case"],[13280,"Case"],[13419,"Case"],[13466,"Case"],[13739,"Case"],[13870,"Case"],[12946,"Case (audio s)"],[13836,"Case (cap)"],[13252,"Case (whole: warm s)"],[16104,"Cast"],[15137,"Catalogue model"],[15239,"Catalogue model"],[15410,"Catalogue model"],[15502,"Catalogue model"],[15738,"Catalogue model"],[15662,"Catalogue models"],[8582,"Catalogue, 