nd"],[10333,"Command"],[10342,"Command"],[10351,"Command"],[10366,"Command"],[10391,"Command"],[10419,"Command"],[10428,"Command"],[10450,"Command"],[10466,"Command"],[10499,"Command"],[10533,"Command"],[10567,"Command"],[10582,"Command"],[10614,"Command"],[10629,"Command"],[16241,"Command"],[16002,"Command line"],[16042,"Command line"],[16109,"Command line"],[16409,"Command line"],[16533,"Command line"],[16713,"Command line"],[8842,"Command line: the same operations in a terminal."],[10056,"Command reference"],[11215,"Command reference: every command's arguments and options."],[15054,"Commit and open PRs only when asked."],[11996,"Commit messages"],[12055,"Commit messages take the form `type(scope): summary`, the summary in lower case, saying what the change does:"],[8763,"Common parameters: `temperature`, `top_p`, `top_k`, `speed`, `seed`, `segment_silence_ms`…"],[9644,"Common questions by topic: starting up, the access token, torch and engines, GPU memory, licences, downloads, logs and remote hosts."],[11131,"Common workflows"],[14487,"Compares the two implementations' training runs; the exported voice or model can be handed to the other implementation to load"],[14483,"Compares two runs sample for sample (`--tolerance`, `--report` writes a Markdown report); prints the current table from the fixtures without running a model. CPU runs compare bit for bit only at the same thread count (CPU kernels split their sums by it): `stack.py` records each run's (`threads`), and the table names both counts where they differ. VoxCPM's fixtures were made with 8 threads (`OMP_NUM_THREADS=8`, `compute.cpu_threads=off`); Mizuoto's default binds one per physical core, 12 on the development machine, where both native and upstream give an output one int16 step away from the fixtures (2026-11-04: identical to each other at 8 and at 12 threads)"],[13371,"Compile cost"],[9844,"Compiled"],[11428,"Compiled module"],[9732,"Compiling models (`compute.compile`)"],[14303,"Components"],[12568,"Components in use by any request are never victims; the running model's components that the current phase does not need are. Each victim gives up units, in reverse fill order, until the shortfall is met (`partially_unload`); in `high` and `shared` it leaves whole. `empty_cache` runs after an eviction, and before a load whose device holds more unused cache than a quarter of its free memory (step 2 above); never per step."],[12496,"Components the phase does not name stay where they are and give up memory first when another phase needs it: an IndexTTS clone of a cached voice never places w2v-BERT or CAM++."],[47,"compute"],[8571,"compute"],[16267,"Compute"],[12402,"Compute attention with `mizuoto.runtime.accel.attention(q, k, v, site=SITE, …)`, never `F.scaled_dot_product_attention` (an architecture test forbids it): declare `SITE = accel.Site(\"<id>.<part>\")` once per call site, and pass the arguments upstream passed to SDPA (`causal` is its `is_causal`). A site where upstream wrote attention by hand gives that code as its `reference`; one that only its reference may compute is `swappable=False` (attentions with relative positions inside the scores are not sites at all: they stay hand-written). Where the site builds a mask from a structure (padding on one side, causal, a window), pass `mask_info` too, so faster kernels can take the call (Acceleration)."],[12664,"Conditions"],[12871,"Configuration"],[10678,"Configuration and environment variables"],[11216,"Configuration and environment variables: settings, environment variables and the data folder."],[11097,"Connect with TLS"],[11535,"Contents"],[16582,"Contents"],[16990,"Contents"],[11987,"Conventions"],[15013,"Conventions that hold everywhere"],[11611,"Conventions:"],[16494,"Convert voice"],[182,"Cookie"],[8706,"Cookie"],[14257,"Cooperative cancel. `check_cancel()` raises `Cancelled`, a `BaseException`, so model code's `except Exception` cannot swallow it. Engines call it at every token or ODE step"],[12553,"Copies are made outside inference mode, in the weights' own dtype, so a streamed layer computes with the same kind of tensor as a resident one (an inference tensor takes other CPU kernels). Each fetch checks for a cancel. A `Compiled` module above a streamed unit runs eagerly (its graph would hold the weights), and CUDA graphs are captured for models wholly on their device, or for a `sequence` handle whose streamed units rest in page-locked memory (`ModelHandle.graphable`; Qwen3-TTS's talker uses it). Captured, each streamed weight's copy is a memcpy node from its fixed host tensor into the graph's own memory, made inside the capture (a copy from the eager run before it is not used: the graph would keep reading that buffer after it is freed) and per leaf, so a layer split across graphs around its attention copies each weight once a step. The streamer counts the replays' copies (`ModelHandle.replayed`), so `meta.memory.streamed_mb` stays right."],[10856,"Copy streams for streamed weights (-1: two on NVIDIA and AMD, none elsewhere; 0: off); autoregressive models never prefetch"],[9809,"copy streams that move streamed weights while the GPU computes (`-1`: two on NVIDIA and AMD, none elsewhere); used for models that run once per input, not for autoregressive ones, where they only cost memory"],[11619,"Core method"],[14526,"Corpus runs in each engine's production dtype and device, native against reference; seeds not aligned (GPU kernels differ)"],[10317,"Correct a clip's transcript"],[10527,"Correct, exclude or delete a clip"],[14516,"Cosine ≥ 0.999"],[730,"CosyVoice"],[1323,"CosyVoice"],[2907,"CosyVoice"],[5406,"CosyVoice"],[6304,"CosyVoice"],[6600,"CosyVoice"],[7322,"CosyVoice"],[7555,"CosyVoice"],[8334,"CosyVoice"],[9254,"CosyVoice"],[9847,"CosyVoice"],[11431,"CosyVoice"],[13930,"CosyVoice"],[14828,"CosyVoice"],[15124,"CosyVoice"],[15846,"CosyVoice"],[16079,"CosyVoice"],[16857,"CosyVoice"],[9279,"CosyVoice (`cosyvoice`)"],[16562,"CosyVoice (300M, 2, 3)"],[9426,"CosyVoice 1 