and `NO_PROXY`. Set them in the environment that starts `mizuoto webui` or `mizuoto model download`."],[1055,"Drama 3"],[6769,"Drama 3"],[9579,"Drama 3"],[15293,"Drama 3"],[14000,"Drama 3 itself, which could not load on this machine before (its 30 GiB of experts beside the rest of the model in 31 GB), with the final code: 21.5 GB of experts in files, 16.3 GB in page-locked RAM, 9.1 GB on the GPU; the first load 81 s; a warm request of 5.5–8.3 s of speech 129–162 s, 176–226 GB copied to the GPU a request (1.4 GB/s; the link carries 2.9); each case's two runs identical; RAM never under 7.9 GB available. Read from the disk in a warm request (`/proc/self/io`): 32.4, 27.8, 15.2 and 17.1 GiB (clone en, clone zh, its own voice with tags, dialogue). With 57 % of the experts in files, about 100–130 GB of a request's reads come from them, so the page cache served 72–87 % of those and the disk 13–28 % (8–15 % of all that was copied). Its contract suite with a reference clip: load, every voice mode in English and Chinese (Whisper's WER under 0.35), seeds and segments, streaming, unloading and no residue pass. Cancelling took 2.0 s against the suite's 2 s, from a cancel that arrived while the backbone was being placed again after the unloading test: copying 9 GB to the GPU and page-locking 17 GB of RAM (44 s on its first placement) check for no cancel; cancelled while generating, it stopped within 0.1 s."],[5476,"Drama 3 本身此前在这台机器上无法加载（31 GB 内存放不下 30 GiB 专家加上模型其余部分），使用最终代码：文件中 21.5 GB 专家，锁页内存中 16.3 GB，GPU 上 9.1 GB；首次加载 81 秒；预热后合成 5.5–8.3 秒语音用时 129–162 秒，每次请求向 GPU 复制 176–226 GB（1.4 GB/s；链路可达 2.9）；每个用例的两次运行完全相同；可用内存从未低于 7.9 GB。预热后一次请求从磁盘读取的量（`/proc/self/io`）：32.4、27.8、15.2 和 17.1 GiB（英文克隆、中文克隆、自带音色加标签、对话）。57% 的专家在文件中，一次请求约有 100–130 GB 从这些文件读取，所以其中 72–87% 由页缓存提供，13–28% 来自磁盘（占全部复制量的 8–15%）。带参考音频的契约测试：加载、英文和中文的每种音色模式（Whisper 的 WER 低于 0.35）、种子与分段、流式输出、卸载、无残留均通过。取消用了 2.0 秒，超过测试的 2 秒：取消发生在卸载测试之后主干重新放置的过程中，向 GPU 复制 9 GB 和锁定 17 GB 内存（首次放置时 44 秒）都不检查取消；生成过程中取消时，它在 0.1 秒内停止。"],[5413,"Drama 3 超出内存预算的专家保存在文件中（`runtime.filemap`，见显存），以及其他地方需要的保护（文件支持的张量从不锁页；`disk_bytes` 与 `host_bytes` 分开计算；流式层复制每一行之前检查取消）。在 vllm_server 的 RTX 3060（12 GB，PCIe x4，内存 31 GB，torch 2.8）上，用 Mizuoto 0.2.36（`10515bc`）与这次改动对比，每个模型一个进程，每次运行两遍（第二遍为预热后），每个引擎按 基线/新/基线/新 交替，使用 G10 用例："],[13937,"Drama 3's experts beyond the RAM budget kept in files (`runtime.filemap`, Memory), with the guards it needs elsewhere (no file-backed tensor is page-locked; `disk_bytes` apart from `host_bytes`; a cancel checked before each row a streamed layer copies). Checked on the vllm_server's RTX 3060 (12 GB, PCIe x4, 31 GB of RAM, torch 2.8), Mizuoto 0.2.36 (`10515bc`) against the change, one model per process, two runs each (the second warm), alternated base/new/base/new per engine, the G10 cases:"],[11515,"Draw with `multinomial1` / `multinomial_draws` and keep decoding steps free of waits (no `.item()`, `tolist()`, Python scalars into tensors, masked assignment) except one per step."],[16441,"Drop audio on **Drop audio files here**, or click it to choose a file (WAV, FLAC, MP3, M4A, OGG…). Or:"],[12387,"Drop the weights (the manager has already taken the handles off their devices)"],[14508,"DSP, samplers, tokenizers, normalisers, g2p"],[15886,"DSP, samplers, tokenizers, normalisers, g2p"],[7362,"DSP、采样器、分词器、文本规范化、g2p"],[5984,"DSP、采样器、分词器、规范化器、字音转换"],[11328,"dtypes"],[6312,"dummy"],[14836,"dummy"],[5879,"dummy 引擎"],[14543,"Duration ratio"],[12201,"E.g. CosyVoice-BlankEN's weights and the semantic codec IndexTTS-2.5 never reads only took space"],[955,"E2-TTS Base"],[9479,"E2-TTS Base"],[6725,"E2-TTS 的 UNetT：带跳连的扁平 transformer，x-transformers 的 RMSNorm"],[15249,"E2-TTS's UNetT: a flat transformer with skip connections, x-transformers' RMSNorm"],[14311,"Each `LocalEngine` is a memory holder: **Free GPU memory** (`POST /api/v1/compute/release`) unloads every model of every idle holder and offloads what is left; refused while a holder is busy"],[15678,"Each 80 ms frame of audio is 16 codes. The **talker**, a 28-layer Qwen3 decoder over text and codec embeddings, predicts the frame's first code; the **code predictor**, a 5-layer transformer, predicts the other 15 one after the other; the sum of the 16 code embeddings (plus the next text token's embedding) is the talker's next input. The **12 Hz codec** turns codes back into 24 kHz audio (1920 samples a frame) and, for cloning, the reference into codes. Base models also have a **speaker encoder** (ECAPA-TDNN) whose embedding sits in the prompt."],[12868,"Each autoregressive decoder launched thousands of small kernels per step one by one and waited for the device many times a step (`torch.multinomial`'s checks, masks copied at each step, padding masks read back, stop checks), so the CPU's launch time and the GPU's work added up. Each now waits once per step and, with `compute.cuda_graphs`, replays its step's kernels as CUDA graphs (Acceleration). Every result below is the old code's audio or tokens; the CPU parity cases of each engine stayed identical. All on the shared GPUs described above."],[14253,"Each call to an engine gets one `RequestContext` (`mizuoto/runtime/context.py`):"],[16730,"Each clip gets a **What is said in the clip** field. It may stay empty: **Missing transcripts are filled by speech recognition when it is installed.**"],[16605,"Each clip’s peak at -1 dBFS"],[11647,"Each command is a plain function, its parameters declared with `Annotated[..., typer.Option(...)]`"],[10030,"Each connection starts with the token, which the agent compares in constant time; a wrong one closes the connection."],[12594,"Each decoder's output samples depend on a bounded window of its input frames, so the tiles need no fade: `context_tiled_1d` decodes each tile (256 frames, 128 for OmniVoice) with the frames that window reaches around it (before it only, for a causal decoder) and keeps the tile's own samples. The decoder computes the bound from its layers (`context_frames()`): Vocos 29 frames each side (its kernels and the inverse STFT's window), IndexTTS 2's BigVGAN 39 each side, VoxCPM's causal VAEs 20–22 before, Fish's causal codec decoder 20 before, HiggsAudio's DAC (OmniVoice) 12 each side. The tiles compute the same function as the whole and differ only in the sums' rounding, measured on 60 s of speech (2026-11-04, `/root/vllm_server/tiles/`):"],[14095,"Each distribution has a version of its own, in a file that holds nothing else; a push to `main` that changes it releases that distribution (see below):"],[12170,"Each distribution has its own version and is checked and released on its own; a gated package names the Mizuoto versions it works with (`mizuoto>=0.2.0,<0.3`)"],[9701,"Each engine's licence is in Engines in depth."],[11861,"Each event in `mizuoto/core/events/models.py` is a `Record` with an `__event_name__`: `job_updated`, `job_log`, `jobs_cleared`, `outputs_added` / `outputs_removed`, `voices_changed`, `models_changed`, `presets_changed`, `engines_changed`, `runtime_changed` (the loaded models and the engines' states, as `RuntimeStatus`), `compute_changed`, `settings_changed`, `datasets_changed`, `projects_changed`, `experiments_changed`, `train_metrics`. `EventBase.get_events()` collects every subclass; `mizuoto/api/openapi.py` writes them into the OpenAPI schema, from which the UI types its socket."],[9045,"Each file goes where Mizuoto's mirror source asks for it. A copy in a models folder with the same size and SHA-256 is hard-linked (else copied); anything else is downloaded from the official sources by Mizuoto's own downloader: resumed, retried and checked against its SHA-256."],[8953,"Each file picks its source on its own:"],[14846,"Each finished stage records a fingerprint, computed by `fingerprints()` and chained in stage order:"],[16311,"Each host shows its state (**Online**, **Offline**, **Refused**), **Devices**, **Installed engines** and **Used by**, and can be changed or removed. **Check again** refreshes every host."],[9980,"Each host shows its state (**Online**, **Offline**, **Refused**), **Devices**, **Installed engines** and **Used by**; **Check again** reconnects at once."],[10037,"Each host's state (`refresh` reconnects)"],[16754,"Each installed model, and whether and how it can use the voice: **Clone**, **Clone (no transcript)**, **Preset speaker**, **Designed** or **Trained**, with badges such as **own weights**, **transcribed first** or **trimmed to fit**; models that cannot say why."],[11449,"each layer's halves around its attention, the slow transformer's 36 sharing one compiled graph per half and the fast transformer's 4 another;"],[16113,"Each line is rendered on its own, and each rendering is a **take**. After you change a line's text, speaker or settings, only that line needs rendering again; at the end the lines are joined, with the pauses you set, into one file with subtitles. Speakers may use models of different engines."],[12024,"Each Mizuoto engine is a port of an upstream project and must give **the same** results: on the CPU in fp32 with the same seed, the audio is identical sample for sample (for trainers: losses, learning rates and saved weights identical byte for byte). This rule decides much of how code is written:"],[9868,"each model as its original implementation did, so results stay identical to it"],[14512,"Each module with real weights on captured inputs"],[15889,"each module with the real weights on captured inputs"],[12279,"Each needs its own hint and exit code"],[11724,"Each operation has exactly one core method, taking and returning `Record` models (`mizuoto/core/record.py`). Routes and commands parse the input, call it and shape the output. Listing presets, for example:"],[8617,"Each operation is one method of the core; the API and the command line only parse, call it and print the result. So the `mizuoto … --json` of a listing or a query prints the JSON its route returns, for example `mizuoto model list --json` and `GET /api/v1/models`. The exception is `mizuoto speak --json`, which prints `{\"job\": …, \"outputs\": […]}`: the job plus the output records."],[11409,"Each optional backend imports its package the first time a policy asks for it on a device, then checks it:"],[14747,"each package in scope × Ubuntu, Windows, macOS × Python 3.10, 3.14"],[14750,"each package in scope, Ubuntu, Python 3.12"],[12186,"Each port matches its reference sample for sample (CPU, fp32, same seed); the reference is how Mizuoto 0.1 actually called upstream, not upstream's demos"],[16211,"Each rendering of a line adds a take and uses it at once. Up to 5 takes are kept per line; older ones not in use are deleted. **Take N** in the line's menu goes back to an earlier one."],[8698,"Each request passes three checks (`mizuoto/api/security.py`):"],[16000,"Each result"],[14996,"Each route's `meta.screen` in `router.ts` names the navigation destination it belongs to; `addressOf(screen)` remembers each destination's last address, so the navigation goes back to the voice or project it left rather than to the list."],[16093,"Each row shows the name, size, description and **used by** *models*. Each can be downloaded or deleted on its own. A model missing a shared file it needs shows as **Partly downloaded**. Shared files are kept in `models/_assets/<engine>/` in the data folder."],[11719,"Each rule has a reason:"],[15114,"Each segment recognised alone, shortest first, as FunASR does on a CPU (`batch_size = 0`); its features with `dither` 1.0 (Paraformer's frontend default)."],[16010,"Each shows its text (or name), length, waveform (click or drag to seek), model, time taken, real-time factor (RTF) and seed, with any warnings and licence notices (such as Fish Speech's \"Built with Fish Audio\"). Its menu:"],[15720,"Each training forward gets a fresh cache: the first `DynamicCache` update concatenates, so attention sees contiguous keys and values, as upstream's."],[16726,"Each voice is a folder under `voices/<name>/` in the data folder (`voice.json` and FLAC clips in `references/`). 