me server files)"],[8765,"Engine-specific options"],[12339,"Engine-specific options (`engine_options`); unknown ones always raise; `group = \"hidden\"` keeps one out of forms. The engine's `OPTION_SCHEMA` must mirror them exactly"],[12716,"Engine, case"],[12788,"Engine, case"],[13055,"Engine, case"],[12831,"Engine, recipe"],[13189,"Engine, recipe"],[50,"engines"],[8574,"engines"],[9361,"Engines"],[15914,"Engines"],[16036,"Engines"],[16809,"Engines"],[12070,"Engines and exactness"],[10079,"Engines and the runtime"],[16310,"Engines can run on other machines: run `mizuoto agent` there (it has its own engines and models), add it here, then choose it as an engine's device under **Models › Engines**. Training stays on this machine."],[12264,"Engines get references as `cache/refs/<sha256>.wav` (16-bit WAV); voices store FLAC"],[12011,"Engines import only `runtime`, `nn`, `text`, `training`, `core.codes`, `core.inference.tasks` and their own package, and **never another engine**. Code two engines share goes into `nn` or `runtime`."],[9248,"Engines in depth"],[14279,"Engines share one process with the server, each other and the tests, so native code **changes nothing process-wide**. `test_native_code_leaves_global_state_alone` forbids, in `runtime`, `nn`, `text`, the engines and the gated packages:"],[12014,"Engines, trainers, the runtime and the server share one process, so code under `runtime`, `nn`, `text`, `engines` and `packages/native` keeps these rules (details in Runtime):"],[10820,"Engines' default device: `auto`, `cpu`, `cuda:N` (NVIDIA, or AMD on ROCm), `xpu:N` (Intel) or `mps`"],[11787,"Entry"],[12407,"Entry points are read once per process: installing such a distribution means restarting Mizuoto. Its package follows the engines' rules and mirrors its manifest (`check_native_package`, `check_options_mirror`, called by its `tests/test_<id>_package.py`), has its own version in `mizuoto_<id>/version.py` with the Mizuoto versions it works with in its `pyproject.toml`