y:"],[9864,"Every attention computation of every engine and trainer goes through one switch, `compute.attention` (**Settings** › **Compute** › **Attention**), after ComfyUI's attention backends:"],[11467,"Every capture also registers the device's default generator and marks it capturing; ending a failed capture does not unmark it, and from then on every draw from it outside a capture raised (\"Offset increment outside graph capture encountered unexpectedly\": `torch.randn` without a generator, dropout, inductor's benchmarks), in every engine, until the process ended. `release_default_generator` captures one kernel that draws nothing, which begins and ends its capture again: its seed and offset are unchanged (`tests/runtime/test_graphs.py`)."],[15969,"Every catalogue model with its engine, size, GPU memory and state, and a **Download** button; see Downloading models"],[16154,"Every change is saved a moment after you stop typing, and when you leave the page; there is nothing to save by hand."],[14916,"Every colour role (`primary`, `on-primary`, `surface-container`, `outline`…) generated from one seed colour with `@material/material-color-utilities`' Tonal Spot scheme, light and dark, at contrast 0 (standard), 0.5 (medium) and 1 (high)"],[10104,"Every command takes these options; the tables leave them out:"],[11555,"Every core error (`mizuoto/core/errors.py`) carries `code`, `http_status` and `exit_code`; `install_error_handlers()` turns any `MizuotoError` into one shape:"],[14457,"Every declared voice mode, in English and Chinese, is audible (RMS > 0.01), at the right rate, about as long as the text needs; with ASR installed, word error rate \\< 0.35"],[15897,"Every engine above is identical at T3, with no error at all, except CosyVoice when each side makes its own voice prompt. Four opt-in paths are held to less: `compute.compile` (within 1e-4, except CosyVoice, whose vocoder amplifies float differences), Qwen3-TTS's `fused_projections` (identical on the CPU, not on a GPU) OmniVoice's `packed_guidance` (identical on the CPU in the parity cases; another take of the request on a GPU) and VoxCPM's `attention_span` (identical on the CPU, another take on a GPU)."],[16697,"Every engine also trains on a CPU, which is enough to check the whole run works with little data and few steps."],[9892,"Every engine and every trainer runs on a CPU, which is fine for trying things and short sentences, but much slower than a GPU, especially for long texts and training (GPT-SoVITS trains in minutes on a GPU and hours on a CPU). Smaller models (Qwen3-TTS 0.6B, GPT-SoVITS) shorten the wait noticeably; `compute.compile` helps F5-TTS most."],[13237,"every engine but Fish Speech (its in-place Snake: below)"],[13235,"every engine but VoxCPM (its attention span: below)"],[11233,"Every engine gives its upstream's output sample for sample on the CPU (see Engines in depth), and speed work keeps it that way: **a default never changes a result**. Faster paths that compute the same kernels with the same arguments (CUDA graphs, fewer waits for the device, CPU memory and thread placement) are on by default. Faster paths that change the arithmetic (other attention kernels, TF32, `torch.compile`, fused projections) are opt-in, and every output lists the ones that ran. Measurements are in Performance record; GPU memory is in Memory."],[15824,"Every engine in Mizuoto is a port: the model code of an upstream project, written again on Mizuoto's runtime (`mizuoto/runtime`) and its shared building blocks (`mizuoto/nn`, `mizuoto/text`). No upstream code is vendored, and no engine imports transformers, onnxruntime or the upstream package. Each port is held to one standard: on the CPU, in fp32, with the same seed, it gives the output of the code it replaces, sample for sample."],[14394,"Every engine is already installed with Mizuoto; a real one needs only its models:"],[9336,"Every engine is implemented in Mizuoto and runs in the server's own process, in the one Python environment Mizuoto is installed in. An engine is **available** when torch imports there and its implementation is installed; `mizuoto doctor` (and **Models** › **Engines**) says which engines are available and, for the others, what is missing and the command that installs it."],[16812,"Every engine is implemented in Mizuoto itself, on its own runtime over torch, and runs inside the server's process; there is one Python environment and nothing to build per engine. Requests, voices, parameters, jobs and results look the same whichever engine serves them."],[14972,"Every engine is installed with Mizuoto, but one can still be *missing* something: torch, or a licence-gated engine's own distribution. The engine list (`EngineStatus.available`, `missing`) and the doctor's report (`useDoctor(engine)` in `api/queries/engines.ts`: `GET /api/v1/engines/{id}/doctor`, or `GET /api/v1/runtime/doctor` for all) drive what the UI offers:"],[15972,"Every engine is part of Mizuoto and runs in the server's own process: there is nothing to install per engine. An engine is **Available** when torch is installed (the dummy engine needs none) and its implementation is there: built in, or for Fish Speech and IndexTTS their own distribution (`mizuoto-fishspeech`, `mizuoto-indextts`). Otherwise its card under **Models › Engines** says **Not available** and what it needs, and the model picker marks its models **Not available**."],[14051,"Every engine is ported in-tree, so none of these upstream dependencies is needed any more:"],[12265,"Every engine reads 16-bit WAV; registering by content avoids duplicates"],[14184,"Every engine runs in the server's own process (or in the command's, on the command line), on Mizuoto's own runtime: `mizuoto/runtime/`, a small framework in the manner of ComfyUI's model management. The core reaches it only through `mizuoto/core/inference/`. This page covers both sides: what an engine gets from the runtime, and how the core calls a loaded model. How to write an engine is in Adding an engine."],[9736,"Every engine runs in the server's own process, on Mizuoto's runtime (torch). The defaults run on any machine. This page covers the settings that decide where models run and how long they stay loaded, the speed-ups you can turn on (attention backends, `compute.fast`, `compute.compile`), and how waiting requests are batched. The defaults keep every result identical to each engine's original implementation; each opt-in that changes results says so. Each engine is described in Engines in depth; every setting is listed in Configuration."],[9359,"Every engine runs on a CPU too, much more slowly. The speed-up option is `compute.compile`, in Performance."],[9692,"Every engine runs on a CPU, much more slowly than on a GPU: the CPU runs in fp32, and large models such as Fish Speech are especially slow. Pick smaller models (Qwen3-TTS 0.6B, the GPT-SoVITS v2 family…), run the engine on a GPU machine as a remote host, or turn on streaming playback to hear the audio as it is made."],[9753,"Every engine runs on NVIDIA (CUDA), AMD (ROCm), Intel (XPU) and Apple (MPS) GPUs and on the CPU. On a GPU without double precision (Apple's, and Intel Arc cards), the one model part that computes in double precision, CosyVoice 3's pitch predictor, runs on the CPU while the rest of the model stays on the GPU. On Apple silicon `compute.compile` is ignored and torch's MPS backend may lack an operation an engine needs; starting Mizuoto with `PYTORCH_ENABLE_MPS_FALLBACK=1` runs such operations on the CPU. The ROCm, XPU and MPS paths are not yet tested on real hardware: please report what fails."],[14120,"every engine's implementation and trainer imported (`get_engine`), every module of `mizuoto` and the gated packages imported, and every data file the checkout has beside the code of the distributions built from it found installed (the ones engines read at run time actually read);"],[12233,"Every engine's models share one process and its memory"],[11863,"Every long operation is a job. Services register a factory with `jobs.register(kind, factory)` when they are built; the factory turns a request (plain JSON) into a `JobSpec`:"],[10057,"Every mizuoto command group and command, grouped by purpose: what it does, its main arguments and options, and an example, taken from each command's --help."],[8935,"Every model in the catalogue names its repository and a pinned files manifest (`mizuoto/core/engines/manifests/files/*.files.json`): the repository's commit and each file's path, size and SHA-256. Mizuoto fetches only the listed files and checks each one's size and SHA-256, so the files are identical whichever source served them."],[12400,"Every module with weights is wrapped in a `ModelHandle` and listed in `self.handles`, so the model manager can place it, offload it and report its size:"],[9034,"every one"],[12631,"Every output's `meta.memory`: `streamed_mb` (copied from RAM during the request), `loaded_mb`, `size_mb`, `host_mb` (its weights kept in RAM: host copies and streamed units) and `pinned_mb` (the page-locked part), `peak_mb` on CUDA and XPU (the most torch held on the device in the request's measured phases: every resident model's weights and the working memory, from the peak the calibration measures; with requests of several calls, the highest), and for partly loaded components `partial`: per component the `reason` (the budget fell short, `vram_mode low` or `none`, capped after running out of memory, or gave up memory for another), the `mode`, `free_mb`, `working_mb` and `reserve_mb` weighed, `loaded_mb`, `size_mb` and `gave_up_for`. The log says the same when it happens."],[12477,"Every registered component, the budget, eviction, partial loading, the OOM retry's clean-up, calibration, reporting"],[12177,"Every required dependency has wheels on every platform CI covers; without an extra, text in that language fails with `capability_not_supported` and the install command"],[8561,"Every REST route is under `/api/v1`:"],[16786,"Every result"],[16839,"Every result: search, favourites, download, run again with the same settings."],[13998,"Every run's audio was identical to 0.2.36's first round (39 comparisons). The differences are within the runs' own spread; none of these models has a file-backed weight, so the only new work on their path is a check of each host tensor's storage when it is pinned. This build had neither the per-row cancel check nor the full-disk guard, added after: the first runs only for row-streamed layers (Drama 3's alone), the second only when a file is made, so neither is on these engines' path; Drama 3 was timed again with the final code (below)."],[12239,"Every site passes `is_causal` as upstream did, and CosyVoice's streamed-text steps rely on the top-left form; the only site with dropout (GPT-SoVITS's T2S training) calls SDPA's own"],[15647,"Every step is a full forward of the conditional and unconditional rows over the whole sequence; there is no CUDA-graph path for this engine."],[11880,"Every synthesis job (`speak`, `convert`, `edit`), on any engine and device; a micro-batch is one job"],[11762,"Every synthesized file and its provenance"],[16231,"Every take is resampled to it (speakers' models may differ in rate)"],[14782,"Every trainable engine trains natively, in Mizuoto's own environment, on the same modules it runs inference with. Each trainer reproduces its upstream recipe: given the same seed on the CPU, its losses, learning rates and saved weights equal byte for byte those of the upstream scripts (as Mizuoto 0.1 ran them; for VoxCPM, upstream's own script). Training needs no environment and no extra of its own: trainers use the modules and dependencies inference uses, without transformers, accelerate, peft, Lightning, Hydra, datasets or webdataset. The host side is `mizuoto/core/training/service.py` (`TrainingService`); the engine side is `mizuoto/training/` (`Trainer`, `StageContext`, `stage.py`) plus each engine's trainer module. Using the Train screen is in Train."],[15876,"Every trainer gives upstream's losses, learning rates and saved weights byte for byte on the CPU when both are seeded alike, and each implementation loads the other's exports (and, but for CosyVoice's voice prompt, speaks them identically). The contract suite (the real models through the whole stack) passes for every engine on the CPU: Qwen3-TTS 24 tests, F5-TTS 12, OmniVoice 12, CosyVoice 18, Fish Speech 6, IndexTTS 18, GPT-SoVITS 24, VoxCPM 18."],[11213,"Every trainer runs in Mizuoto's own environment; each stage runs as a child process of the same Python."],[12518,"every unit streams: the fixed parts and the copies in flight only"],[16440,"Every voice in the picker carries badges saying how **this model** can use it: **Clone**, **Clone (no transcript)**, **Preset speaker**, **Designed** and so on; and when more is needed, **transcribed first** (the clip has no transcript, so it is transcribed before speaking) or **trimmed to fit** (the clip is too long and will be cut). Voices the model cannot use are greyed, with the reason. With an empty library, **New voice** is offered."],[14736,"everything"],[12269,"Everything between the machine and the engines is said in one place"],[14362,"Everything CI runs: `lint`, `typecheck-py`, `test-py`, `test-web`, `typegen-check`"],[8910,"Everything Mizuoto writes is in `/data`: `settings.toml`, the database, models, shared files, voices, outputs, datasets, experiments, projects, caches and logs. The image itself holds no state, so a rebuilt image keeps working on the same volume."],[11807,"Everything the core knows about model code is in `mizuoto/core/inference/`:"],[12449,"Eviction"],[12906,"Exact"],[13571,"Exact"],[12919,"Exact (default)"],[9290,"exact duration, speech editing"],[11992,"Exactness"],[15829,"Exactness (CPU, fp32, same seed)"],[15950,"Exactness is established on the CPU. GPU runs are checked for identical results between Mizuoto's own fast and plain paths, not sample for sample against 