e/`, `jobs/` (job logs) and `logs/`."],[16142,"It imports as one chapter of six lines: \"Anna\" and \"Old man\" each begin two lines and become two new speakers; the other lines are the narrator's; the first line, the dialogue and the last line are three paragraphs."],[9010,"It is not pinned to a commit, but each file is checked against the manifest's size and SHA-256 like any other; a file that does not match comes from the official repository."],[9889,"it is not streamed text input;"],[16124,"It means"],[14857,"It moves the real stdout aside for events and points file descriptor 1 at stderr, so whatever libraries print goes to the log, not into the event stream. Events are JSON lines prefixed with `@mizuoto ` (`mizuoto/core/jobs/jsonl.py`), and records of the `mizuoto` loggers become `LogEvent`s."],[9862,"It needs a working C++ compiler. Without one, or when a model's code cannot be compiled, Mizuoto logs one warning and runs that model as before. The Docker image has none, so there it changes nothing."],[9049,"It reads `MIRROR.json` (from `build` or `mirror_fetch.py`) and writes:"],[9085,"It sends a HEAD request to each catalogue file's URL, the one Mizuoto itself would download, and prints `complete` or the number of missing files per model; the exit code is 1 when anything is missing."],[14392,"It starts the API as `python -m mizuoto webui --no-open --port 7869 --strict-port` (with the repository root on `PYTHONPATH`) and Vite as `bun run dev`, passing `MIZUOTO_BACKEND=http://127.0.0.1:7869` to Vite. Vite proxies `/api` and `/ws` to the API, so the browser only opens `http://localhost:5173`. UI changes reload in place; Python changes, an engine's included, need the task restarted (models load into the server's process). While the API is down, Vite's proxy prints one short line every few seconds instead of a flood of connection errors."],[11443,"It traces with its policy's `trace_run` (a compiled graph cannot read a context variable), one compiled call at a time