ead their fused projections directly; it is small, about 150 MB). A voice's own weights are switched in with `ModelHandle.replace`. The GPT's working memory is sized by the batch's longest row (its phones, the reference's codes and 16 codes a phone, within upstream's 1500 steps). With `compute.oom_fallback`, a batch that runs out of memory is spoken one text at a time."],[15333,"Phases: the codec encodes references and decodes each batch of frames; the language model (`kind=\"sequence\"`, the fast transformer `hot`) generates each batch, placed again as generation resumes. Each batch's working memory is the slow model's cache for its true bound: the references' codes, every text token, the frames of the batches before it and `max_new_tokens`, within `max_seq_len`. S2 Pro took 10.2 GB of GPU memory at most with the defaults (bf16; G13 on Performance); with less, the runtime streams part of its weights. If the codec's decoding runs out of memory with `compute.oom_fallback` on, its convolution decoder runs in tiles of 256 latent frames (about 3 s), each after the 20 frames its first sample depends on (the decoder is causal), and the quantizer's side whole: the whole's samples up to the sums' rounding (40 dB SNR in bf16 on a GPU, where bf16 against float32 is 37.9 dB), in 275 MB instead of 5 GB for 60 s."],[15206,"Phases: the frontend (speech tokenizer and CAM++) only for a voice that is not cached and for conversion; the language model (`kind=\"sequence\"`) makes the tokens; the flow and HiFT speak them. Streaming holds the language model and the flow together. HiFT's F0 predictor is marked `fixed` (HiFT reads its device). The language model's working memory is its cache for upstream's bound (20 speech tokens a text token after a 300-position prompt), at the KV width the model has (Qwen2's two KV heads), with one layer's copy repeated per head group, plus 512 MB. `compute.kv_cache = static` gives the Qwen2 model preallocated caches (identical on the CPU)."],[15794,"Phases: the VAE encodes a voice prompt and decodes; the model (`kind=\"sequence\"`; the local encoder and DiT `hot`, since they run many times a patch) generates; streaming holds both. If the VAE runs out of memory with `compute.oom_fallback` on, it decodes in tiles of 256 latent frames, each after the 20–22 frames its first sample depends on (the decoder is causal): the whole's samples up to the sums' rounding."],[15559,"Phases: w2v-BERT, CAM++, the semantic codec and the regulator for a voice that is not cached (or w2v-BERT for an emotion clip); the emotion model for an emotion text; the GPT (`kind=\"sequence\"`; its GPT-2 `Conv1D` layers stream like linear layers); the s2mel; BigVGAN. A clone of a cached voice never places w2v-BERT or CAM++. If BigVGAN runs out of memory with `compute.oom_fallback` on, it decodes in tiles of 256 frames, each with the 39 frames its samples depend on each side: the whole's samples up to the sums' rounding (IndexTTS 2/2.5). The GPT's working memory is sized by each segment: its text tokens and 24 codes a token (speech runs at about 5), within `max_mel_tokens`, for every beam, in the dtype it computes in."],[9690,"pick a smaller model (Qwen3-TTS 0.6B, for one)."],[14374,"Pin the catalogue models' files (sizes, SHA-256) (`scripts/model_manifests.py`)"],[13801,"Pinned in place"],[9107,"Pinned settings"],[9218,"Pinned settings, shaped like `settings.toml`"],[9126,"Pinned settings, shaped like `settings.toml`; never written to the file"],[16586,"Plain audio files"],[16407,"Plan, Speak and Stream"],[12267,"Planning should not wait on a model, but the result must be usable"],[11771,"Planning, `speak` / `convert` / `edit` jobs, streaming"],[14082,"Platforms"],[11223,"Policies"],[9945,"Port"],[10607,"Port (default from settings: `7870`)"],[12064,"Port selection"],[15613,"Post-processing without pydub (`Segment`: pydub's millisecond arithmetic on int16 arrays, `audioop.rms`)"],[15758,"Precision: `auto` is upstream's choice, the config's bf16 on 