,[16212,"Takes are FLAC results and are not listed in History. Deleting a line, a chapter or the project deletes their takes."],[13074,"talker 0.76, codec decoder 0.03"],[4550,"talker 0.76、codec decoder 0.03"],[13067,"talker 1.22, codec decoder 0.05"],[4543,"talker 1.22、codec decoder 0.05"],[12727,"talker 19.9, codec decoder 0.9"],[4203,"talker 19.9，codec decoder 0.9"],[12723,"talker 30.2, codec decoder 4.0"],[4199,"talker 30.2，codec decoder 4.0"],[7164,"talker 和 code predictor，基于 `runtime/lm/qwen.py`"],[7183,"talker 的工作内存按请求估算：每行的提示（指令、参考文本和编码、文本）加上每个文本 token 16 帧（实际语音约 3–4 帧），不超过 `max_new_tokens`，缓存峰值按比其大小多一层计，再加 256 MB。所以在 1.7B 模型上一句话只预留约 300–400 MB，而不是按最坏情况（8192 帧）要求的数 GB，显存紧张时 talker 也不会被无谓地流式加载。`compute.kv_cache = static` 为 talker 和 code predictor 提供预分配的缓存（CPU 上结果相同）。"],[14359,"Task"],[12293,"Task types"],[14203,"Task types"],[8027,"Teach it a speaker"],[16551,"Teach it a speaker"],[14518,"Teacher-forced logits; discrete outputs from captured inputs (speech-tokenizer codes, VQ codes, ODE trajectories with injected noise)"],[15892,"teacher-forced logits; discrete outputs from captured inputs (speech-tokenizer codes, VQ codes)"],[11419,"TensorFloat-32 matrix products and cuDNN convolutions (NVIDIA, Ampere on)"],[2895,"TensorFloat-32 矩阵乘法和 cuDNN 卷积（NVIDIA，Ampere 及以后）"],[14452,"Test"],[14943,"Test"],[14400,"Testing"],[12310,"Tests"],[11994,"Tests a change needs"],[11796,"Tests build fully isolated services with `environ=` (instead of `os.environ`), `data_dir=` and `settings_overrides=` (`make_services` in `tests/conftest.py`). The dummy engine runs in the test's own process, as every engine does."],[14438,"Tests that need the scheduler and the reaper pass `start_background=True`. The API tests do: `create_app(make_services(start_background=True), bound_host=\"127.0.0.1\", serve_ui=False)`, then `TestClient`."],[12439,"Tests: `tests/engines_native/test_<id>_tiny.py` (an engine in its own distribution keeps them in its package's `tests/`, as `packages/native/<pkg>/tests/` do); the engine id list in `tests/core/test_engines.py::test_registry_lookups` and the `engines` override in `tests/engines/test_contract.py`."],[14034,"Text"],[16403,"Text"],[10242,"Text to look for in names, descriptions and tags (`list`)"],[15759,"Text tokens and audio patches share one sequence. Per patch, a **text-semantic language model** (MiniCPM-4 with LongRoPE and a static KV cache) and a shallower **residual acoustic language model** produce two hidden states; a **local DiT** (a bidirectional MiniCPM-4 run as a conditional flow, about 10 Euler steps with classifier-free guidance) predicts the next patch of latents from them and the previous patch; a **local encoder** embeds the patch back into the language model; a **stop head** decides whether to continue. The **AudioVAE**, a DAC-like causal convolutional codec with Snake activations, decodes the latents (v2 with sample-rate conditioning, 16 kHz latents to 48 kHz audio)."],[15116,"Text: special tokens dropped, English sub-words joined, runs of single letters made one upper-case word; the segments' texts joined without a space between Chinese characters; CT-Transformer over 20-word mini-sentences, carrying the words after each mini-sentence's last stop into the next, and its rules (a space before an ASCII word at a mini-sentence's start, capitalisation after a full stop, a final `。` added)."],[14434,"That is how cancellation at the next check, OOM becoming `compute_unavailable`, timeouts, unloading, the reaper and streamed chunks are all checked in seconds on a CI machine without a GPU. The dummy engine is also how users try Mizuoto out, and `smoke_wheels.py` uses it."],[12215,"That is the weights' licence; the non-commercial term is conveyed by tags and a notice"],[14728,"that package's `gated` and `oldest-mizuoto` jobs, and `torch` for it"],[10736,"The \"UI\" column names the place in the web UI's **Settings**; engine settings are on the engine's card in **Models** › **Engines**."],[16576,"The **Add clips** part of a dataset's page offers several sources:"],[16213,"The **Export** tab:"],[16745,"the **Main clip** badge, or **Make it the main clip**. The main clip comes first when the voice is cloned, and is the one played from the list."],[17041,"The **Speak** button at the bottom is replaced by the one step the model still needs, here **Download Qwen3-TTS 1.7B CustomVoice (size)**. Click it and wait for the progress bar. (When torch is missing, it shows the command that installs it instead.)"],[16450,"The **Text** box takes up to 20,000 characters. Ctrl+Enter in it speaks."],[14941,"The `/dev` route (`DevComponentsView.vue`) shows every `ui/` component, for checking them by eye."],[14132,"The `Dockerfile` at the repository root builds one image: the server, its web UI and every engine, with GPT-SoVITS's Japanese and Korean front ends (and IndexTTS-2.5's Japanese with `GATED=1`). Models go into the `/data` volume."],[8856,"The `Dockerfile` at the repository's root builds one image with the Mizuoto server, its web UI and every engine, torch included; models download into the data volume."],[14883,"The `export` stage returns `{\"artifacts\": [...]}`, which the host's `_register` takes in:"],[10733,"The `MIZUOTO_` prefix is dropped and the rest lower-cased; `__` (two underscores) goes one level down: `MIZUOTO_COMPUTE__GPU_JOBS` is `compute.gpu_jobs`, `MIZUOTO_ENGINES__QWEN3TTS__DEVICE` is `engines.qwen3tts.device`, `MIZUOTO_REMOTE__AGENT__PORT` is `remote.agent.port`."],[11141,"The `mizuoto` command line does what the web UI does: speak, clone and design voices, convert and edit recordings, transcribe, check torch and the engines, manage models, presets, projects, datasets and training, remote hosts, jobs and settings. It is a thin wrapper: each command parses its arguments, calls the **one** core method for that operation and prints the result. The HTTP API behind the web UI calls the same methods, so both behave alike, and the records `--json` prints have the same shape as the API's JSON."],[14227,"The `ModelManager` (`manager.py`, ComfyUI's `load_models_gpu` / `free_memory`) keeps every registered handle with its owner (`<model id>@<device>`) and last use, and places handles **whole or partly** for each phase of a request (`ctx.use`, `ctx.run`): idle components give up memory unit by unit, a model that does not fit keeps part of its weights in RAM and streams them to the device as its layers run, and a phase that runs out of memory runs again, exactly, with more weights streamed. The policy (`policy.py`, `VramPolicy`) comes from the `compute` settings at each load."],[11789,"The `open_services()` context manager (the CLI's through `cli/output.py`), built once per command and closed after"],[15095,"The `paraformer` variant (catalogue model `asr/paraformer-zh`, weights Apache-2.0) is FunASR's `AutoModel(model=paraformer-large, vad_model=fsmn-vad, punc_model=ct-punc).generate(input=path)`, the \"达摩 ASR\" GPT-SoVITS's `tools/asr/funasr_asr.py` uses for Chinese: Mandarin with English words, punctuated, numbers in characters. Code: `mizuoto/engines/asr/paraformer`, ported from FunASR 1.4.21 (MIT). `tts.asr_model_zh = \"asr/paraformer-zh\"` makes it the recogniser for clips whose language is Chinese once it is downloaded (`AsrService.model_for`); Whisper keeps every other language."],[10713,"The `paths.*` settings move models, voices, outputs, datasets, experiments, projects and caches elsewhere one by one; empty means inside the data folder, and so does a relative folder (`results` is `<data folder>/results`, whatever folder Mizuoto is started from)."],[14138,"The `python:<version>-slim` base of the wheels stage and the image"],[14900,"The `ui/` wrapper layer"],[8816,"The `X-Mizuoto-Sample-Rate` header is the rate and `X-Mizuoto-Job` the job (the result is still stored). Streaming text is not available this way."],[15540,"The 1.5/2 front end: WeTextProcessing's FSTs through kaldifst (`TnProcessor`), `TextNormalizer`, SentencePiece, `split_segments`"],[15692,"The 12 Hz speech tokenizer: a Mimi-style encoder (transformers' `MimiModel` encode path) and a causal decoder (72-frame attention window, SnakeBeta upsampling)"],[15542,"The 2.5 front end: punctuation map, normalisation, fugashi for Japanese, tiktoken with `<\\|lang\\|>`"],[15315,"The 44.1 kHz codec"],[9616,"the above plus **Emotion from a clip**, **Emotion sliders**, **Emotion from text**, **Streaming**"],[9445,"the above plus **Preset speakers** (no inline tags)"],[11103,"The address this machine listens on as an agent; `0.0.0.0` for every interface"],[9197,"The address to bind"],[16284,"The address to listen on (`127.0.0.1` by default: this machine only) and the port (7869 by default). **Takes effect the next time the server starts.**"],[16972,"The address to listen on, `127.0.0.1` by default: this machine only"],[10046,"The advanced section is for readers who already use Mizuoto and want to know more about the engines, the API, remote hosts, performance, downloads, containers and calling it from Python."],[14318,"The agent answers each operation with `progress`, `chunk` (a binary frame: float32 little-endian mono) and `file` frames, then a `result` or `error`, and beats every 5 s. With no frame for `remote.heartbeat_timeout` (60 s), the host closes the session with `worker_failed` (`during = \"heartbeat\"`); the next request reconnects."],[10029,"The agent beats every 5 s while it works; a request whose agent stays silent this long fails"],[9996,"The agent cannot be reached"],[8917,"The agent has its own volume and models; build its image like the host's (same Mizuoto version, `GATED=1` if it serves the gated engines). The image's health check asks the web UI's port 7869, which an agent does not serve, hence `--no-healthcheck`. Without TLS, requests and audio cross the network unencrypted: use a trusted network, or give a certificate with `--ssl-certfile` / `--ssl-keyfile` (mount the files into the container)."],[9962,"The agent