eAttention 1.0.6) every backend was checked on every site's recorded calls, through every engine and every trainer: the results and what they decided. SageAttention 3 (Blackwell) is not checked."],[10618,"The remote hosts: address, state, version, devices, engines, the engines using it"],[16524,"The report"],[9072,"The repository to check"],[14175,"The request context"],[14263,"The request's `random.Random`, seeded the same way"],[14261,"The request's `torch.Generator` on a device, one per device, seeded with the request's seed (fresh entropy without one)"],[12574,"the request's generators, its `rng` and any the engine names (`generators=`) are put back as they were before the first attempt;"],[12389,"The requests and results are standard-library dataclasses in `mizuoto/core/inference/tasks.py`, re-exported by `mizuoto.runtime.engine`:"],[16845,"The REST API, a WebSocket for events and streamed audio, an OpenAI-compatible `/v1/audio/speech`, and Python."],[14501,"The result: on the CPU in fp32, every engine is identical to its reference (VoxCPM in bf16 too), except CosyVoice when each side makes its own voice prompt: CAM++'s speaker embedding differs from onnxruntime's by about 1e-6, and HiFT's sine source accumulates and amplifies that along the utterance; given the same voice prompt, CosyVoice is identical sample for sample too. Every trainer gives upstream's losses, learning rates and weights byte for byte on the CPU when both are seeded alike."],[12173,"The right build depends on the hardware and driver, which no package manager can choose for the user"],[13250,"The rotary tables, IndexTTS's in-place GELU and Fish Speech's Snake give their reference's bits on CUDA in fp32, fp16 and bf16 (the exactness tests now run on CUDA when a GPU is visible); CosyVoice's U-Net mask is the same tensor made once. Fish Speech's GPU training replays upstream's initialisation on the CPU generator, as upstream builds its model on the CPU."],[15615,"The rule-based duration estimate, upstream's tables"],[12249,"The run holds the device once; the UI and the fingerprints know the stages without running anything"],[10549,"The run's memory plan before it starts: the device it takes, roughly what it holds there under each `training.memory` setting against the free memory now, and the setting or smaller batch that would fit"],[10019,"The running request fails; the next one reconnects"],[9891,"The running request takes the queued requests of its group just before calling the engine; when the batch fails, they go back to the queue and run one by one. The command line runs one job at a time in the foreground, so only the server (web UI, HTTP API) batches."],[14171,"The runtime"],[12404,"The runtime finds an implementation by id (`get_engine` in `mizuoto/runtime/engine.py`):"],[11526,"The runtime routes"],[12309,"The runtime, in the server's process"],[11436,"the s2mel DiT and BigVGAN (also turned on by its load option `use_torch_compile`)"],[9852,"the s2mel DiT and BigVGAN (also turned on by the load option `use_torch_compile`)"],[13712,"the same"],[13877,"the same"],[13882,"the same"],[13887,"the same"],[13892,"the same"],[13897,"the same"],[13902,"the same"],[13907,"the same"],[13912,"the same"],[8529,"The same as the command line"],[13053,"The same changes help the CPU a little: Qwen3-TTS `cv-en-aiden` 17.05 → 16.76 s, `base-clone-en` 26.19 → 25.83 s, audio identical."],[9683,"The same check shows in **Settings** › **Compute**. \"sees no GPU: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES hides them\" means the variable is set where Mizuoto starts."],[15713,"The same codes as eager; on the decode loop of the 1.7B sizes 2.7–3.4 times faster than the loop with its waits."],[9827,"The same for CosyVoice 2 and 3's language model: about 1 % faster on a GPU, 2–5 % with `fp16`; may be no longer bit-identical there"],[9791,"the same for one engine's models (`auto`: the global setting). UI: **GPU memory for this engine** on its card"],[17023,"The same from the command line"],[16135,"the same name begins two or more lines;"],[12786,"the same operations in the same order"],[12864,"the same operations in the same order"],[11806,"The same path has a few more entrances, all ending in `TtsService`'s one planning and one job: streamed output (a `StreamSink`: the WebSocket `/api/v1/tts/stream`, `POST /tts/speak?stream=true`, `mizuoto speak --stream`), streamed text input (a `TextFeed`, for variants with `stream_text_input`), voice conversion and speech editing (the `convert` and `edit` jobs), and the OpenAI-compatible `POST /v1/audio/speech` (`TtsService.from_openai` maps the model, voice, `instructions`, `speed` and format onto a `SpeakRequest`). The protocols and examples are in HTTP API."],[14459,"The same seed repeats sample for sample; two sentences that do not fit one segment become two segments (or the engine handles long text itself)"],[12784,"the same tensor"],[12782,"the same values"],[12862,"the same values"],[14199,"The same, for a device named `<host>/<device>`: a session with `mizuoto agent` on another machine"],[11313,"the same, or `inherit`"],[15767,"The scalar quantiser, the local encoder, the local DiT (v1 and v2), the CFM's Euler sampler, the prompt sequence, `PatchDecoder` and the generation loop"],[12057,"The scope is the part affected: `runtime`, `webui`, `training`, `models`, `scripts`, `site`, or an engine id (`qwen3tts`, `gptsovits`…); several may be listed (`runtime,training`), or none for a change across the board."],[16768,"The screens"],[16098,"The script format"],[16136,"the script is a dialogue (some name meets one of the two rules above) and the prefix **looks like a name**: it starts with a letter and has at most three words, such as `Dr. Watson` or `林黛玉`."],[9960,"The second line lists the engines available there. Later starts reuse the saved token; to see it again, open that machine's `settings.toml` (`mizuoto config path`)."],[11785,"The server (`mizuoto webui`)"],[8544,"The server `mizuoto webui` starts serves the web UI and an HTTP API. The web UI does everything through this API, so scripts and other programs can do the same things."],[8802,"The server answers `{\"type\": \"queued\", \"job_id\": …}`."],[12122,"The server decides whether a port is free by **binding** it, not by connecting to it (`bind_first_free_port` in `mizuoto/core/net/ports.py`):"],[12118,"The server finds `dist/` through the package's `__path__` (`web_dist_dir()` in `api/static.py`): one line for a source checkout, an installed wheel and a container. `SPAStaticFiles` is mounted last, so it only receives paths the API, the socket and the docs did not match. Without a build it logs a warning and serves the API only, which is the normal state while working on the back end."],[8909,"The server in the container binds `0.0.0.0`, where Mizuoto no longer checks the `Host` header: anyone who reaches the port can do everything (download models, delete files). Set a token with `MIZUOTO_SERVER__ACCESS_TOKEN`, or publish the port on this machine only: `-p 127.0.0.1:7869:7869`."],[8775,"The server pushes events over socket.io at `/ws` (socket.io path `/ws/socket.io`). Traffic is server to client only: every operation goes through REST, REST is the truth, and events only tell you when to refresh."],[14122,"the server: `/api/v1/app/health`, the UI, and a dummy speak through the API."],[9715,"The server's log"],[9099,"The services"],[9237,"The services the server uses (see above), callable once started"],[9880,"The setting applies to models loaded after the change."],[16993,"The settings file (`mizuoto config path` prints its path)"],[9123,"The settings file itself; wins over `config_dir`"],[9194,"The settings file's full path; wins over `config_dir`"],[15220,"the SFT Chinese case and the v2 Chinese clone differ in length, from normalisation; with normalisation off on both sides the first is identical and the second differs only by CAM++'s noise;"],[10395,"The shared assets and the models that need them"],[11501,"The shared Qwen decoder, without autograd, norms and rotates q and k together on the CPU (on a GPU apart, as transformers does, unless the projections are fused: CUDA sizes a reduction by its tensor, so the joined norm differed in the last bit now and then) and uses `F.rms_norm` where a self-test on the device shows the same bits as the float32-upcast norm (`_fused_norm_exact`: one kernel instead of eight on CUDA in bf16/fp16 with recent torch). `mask_for(padded=…)` skips its device check when the caller knows there is no padding."],[11400,"the site refuses quantised attention (`approx_ok=False`: every autoregressive model's, the Qwen decoder's, IndexTTS's GPT, VoxCPM's MiniCPM, GPT-SoVITS's T2S, Fish Speech's three, Whisper's) and the backend is approximate (SageAttention 2 and 3);"],[12092,"The skeleton is GPL-3.0, and so is Mizuoto (`GPL-3.0-only`). The two licence-gated engines ship apart because of their licences (see the decisions below)."],[12079,"The skeleton itself: all logic in `core` with two thin entrances over it (FastAPI and Typer), `build_services()` assembling the services, the `Record` base, domain errors carrying an HTTP status and an exit code, three settings layers (host overrides > environment > file), the event bus and the socket bridge, the security middleware, port binding and `server.json`, `embed.py` for embedding, `scripts/dev.py`, and the layer rule held by a test"],[12085,"The skeleton under machine-learning load: a job queue with named resources and priorities, persisted requests and retry, job workers with JSON-lines events, memory holders and release after running out of memory, a voice library, training experiments with stage fingerprints; the Material 3 front end (`theme/`, `ui/`, motion, layers, shell, stores, i18n, rule tests); the documentation site"],[12116,"The skeleton's existing front end"],[11480,"the slow step around its attention (`LayerSteps`); the draws and the fast transformer one graph; kept per loaded model"],[9856,"the small operations of each decoding step"],[11633,"The socket only pushes changes. The client patches or invalidates the queries an event affects and refetches what is on screen after a reconnect; every state must be readable over REST."],[16396,"The Speak screen: choose a model and a voice, type the text, set the style and parameters, look at the plan, speak or stream, and use the results."],[10969,"The speech recognition model"],[10546,"The stages and exports"],[12860,"the state equals drawing's byte for byte (tested from 1 to 2·10⁹ draws)"],[14920,"The static tokens: the 15 type styles (`--md-sys-typescale-*`, on the Roboto Flex variable font), corner shapes (`--md-sys-shape-corner-*`), motion easings and durations (`--md-sys-motion-*`), state-layer opacities (hover 8 %, focus 10 %, pressed 10 %, dragged 16 %, from `@material/web` 2.5.0's token file; disabled content 38 %, container 12 %, from its component tokens), shadows, spacing (on a 4px unit), in-page z-order and widths that grow with the window; and fallback colours for the first paint"],[11451,"the step's embeddings and heads;"],[11492,"the T2S's one-token steps around each layer's attention, a set per number of rows; sampling eager"],[16537,"The tabs at the top switch between **Experiments** and **Datasets**; at the right is **New experiment** or **New dataset**."],[16004,"The takes of a project's lines are **not** listed here; they are managed on the project's page (see Projects). Files **exported** from a project or a chapter are listed."],[15688,"The talker and the code predictor, on `runtime/lm/qwen.py`"],[15707,"The talker's working memory is estimated from the request: each row's prompt (instruction, reference text and codes, text) and 16 frames per text token (speech runs at 3–4), within `max_new_tokens`, the cache's peak counted as one layer above its size, plus 256 MB. A sentence therefore sets aside some 300–400 MB on the 1.7B model, not the gigabytes a worst case (8192 frames) would claim, so the talker is not streamed needlessly when memory is short. `compute.kv_cache = static` gives the talker and the code predictor preallocated caches (identical on the CPU)."],[10201,"The target voice (a library voice)"],[11811,"The task types engines take and give (`SynthesisTask`, `VoiceSpec`, `LoadSpec`, `AudioChunk`, `Description`, `OptionSpec`…), standard-library dataclasses re-exported by `runtime.engine`; the core builds them at module level without loading the runtime"],[14754,"The tests in scope against the oldest torch Mizuoto supports and the newest, to catch torch's API drift"],[15252,"The text (reference transcript plus the new text, Chinese characters turned into pinyin with tones) is embedded by ConvNeXtV2 blocks; the transformer predicts the flow from noise to mel frames, conditioned on the reference's mel; an ODE solver integrates it over a fixed time grid, with classifier-free guidance as a batch of two; Vocos turns the mel into 24 kHz audio. There is no duration model: the length comes from the reference's speaking rate, or from `duration`."],[15450,"The text-to-semantic model: batched and row-by-row decoding, upstream's sampler"],[10118,"The text; `-` reads it from standard input"],[8753,"The text; `texts` is a batch, one result per text (models that take batches)"],[15188,"The three flows; CosyVoice 3's DiT estimator"],[15186,"The three language models, repetition-aware sampling (RAS), the streamed-text interleave (5 text : 15 speech)"],[14985,"The token (localStorage and the `mizuoto_token` cookie), whether one is needed"],[10609,"The token hosts must give (default from settings; made and saved when there is none)"],[11109,"The token hosts must give; `mizuoto agent` makes one when there is none"],[9949,"The token hosts must give; made and saved when there is none"],[14898,"The token layer: `src/theme/`"],[15771,"The tokenizer as transformers 5.3 builds it, upstream's split of multi-character Han tokens, the text normaliser"],[16493,"The Tools screen: say a recording in another voice with CosyVoice, and replace words in a recording with F5-TTS."],[16766,"The top bar"],[16743,"The top shows the name and kind; a designed voice also shows **Designed with** *model* and its description, a preset voice **Speaker** *name* **of** *model*."],[16935,"The torch build: another CUDA (`cu126`…`cu132`), ROCm (`rocm6.4`…`rocm7.2`) or `cpu` index"],[17027,"The torch builds for AMD, Intel, Apple silicon and the CPU, installing from source and Docker are in Installation."],[8877,"The torch requirement, such as `torch==2.8.0`"],[16938,"The torch requirement, such as `torch==2.8.0`"],[11483,"the tower around its 13 layers' attention, then the backbone around its 10 softmax attention layers (`Stretches`); the tower's again per sampling settings; not when the experts stream"],[14775,"The train job"],[16518,"The Train screen: build and prepare datasets, then run each engine's own fine-tuning recipe stage by stage in experiments, with losses and previews, exported as a voice's weights or a new model."],[14802,"The trainer class is the engine's `TRAINER = \"module:Class\"` (see Adding an engine). `TrainingService.methods(model)` says for each method whether it can start from that model and, if not, the `reason`: disabled, wrong variant, the engine runs on a remote host, the model is not installed, the engine is not available, it has no trainer, the device kind does not fit, the trainer's `REQUIRES` do not import, training assets are missing. Each reason carries the command that fixes it."],[15221,"the training cross-load cases (one implementation's export spoken by the other): 57.4 and 38.1 dB."],[12230,"The training memory tools offer what keeps results and a few things that change them slightly; no Adafactor, no splitting micro-batches on out-of-memory"],[15031,"The two licence-gated engines are separate distributions only because of their licences. They install into the same environment and register themselves under the Python entry-point group `mizuoto.engines`."],[12121,"The UI is built before the wheel: `scripts/build_wheels.py` runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile` and `bun run build`, then builds the sdist and the wheel; Docker builds it in a bun stage of its own, and the final image carries no Node toolchain. See Release."],[14912,"The UI is built on Material Design 3 (M3) in two layers: a **token layer** that everything reads, and a **component layer** on top of it. The token layer depends on no component library; the component layer can be replaced piece by piece."],[17029,"The UI opens on **Speak**; nothing has to be set up before you try it. Two settings are worth a look before downloading a real model:"],[15961,"The UI opens on **Speak**. Nothing has to be set up first: the dummy engine works right away (it speaks in tones), so you can look around before downloading anything. Three places matter for a real engine:"],[16789,"The UI opens on the screen you were last on. Each screen keeps its state (and scroll position) while you visit others; the page of each voice, dataset, experiment and project keeps its own."],[12133,"The UI uses Material Design 3 in two layers:"],[16280,"The UI's language; **Auto** follows the browser"],[12459,"The user-facing settings are in Performance; the runtime as a whole in Runtime."],[11654,"The usual shape of a command (`commands/projects.py`):"],[15456,"The v4/v5 48 kHz HiFi-GAN; the ERes2NetV2 speaker-verification embedding"],[12593,"the VAE's decoder in tiles with context"],[9240,"The values in `settings` sit above the settings file and the environment, are **never written to the file**, and cannot be changed through the web UI or the API:"],[15676,"The variant comes from `config.json` (`tts_model_type`, `tts_model_size`); only `tokenizer_type = qwen3_tts_tokenizer_12hz` is accepted. The model folder holds `config.json`, `model.safetensors`, the tokenizer files (`tokenizer.json`, or `vocab.json` + `merges.txt` + `tokenizer_config.json`) and `speech_tokenizer/` (`config.json`, `model.safetensors`). A Base voice's cache is `prompt.pt`, the clone prompt (reference codes and speaker embedding)."],[15433,"The variant comes from the base GPT and SoVITS pair in the model folder, laid out as upstream lays it out: `gsv-v2final-pretrained/…`, `s1v3.ckpt`, `v2Pro/s2Gv2Pro.pth` / `s2Gv2ProPlus.pth`, `gsv-v4-pretrained/{s2Gv4,vocoder}.pth`, `gsv-v5-pretrained/{s2Gv5turbo,vocoder}.pth`. A voice's own weights (`Voice.weights[\"gptsovits\"]`: a GPT `.ckpt` and a SoVITS `.pth`, version read from the file) replace the base pair for that voice."],[15172,"The variant comes from the yaml in the folder (`cosyvoice.yaml`, `cosyvoice2.yaml`, `cosyvoice3.yaml`); a CosyVoice 1 folder with `spk2info.pt` is SFT or Instruct. The folder holds the yaml, `llm.pt`, `flow.pt`, `hift.pt`, `campplus.onnx`, `speech_tokenizer_v1.onnx` / `v2` / `v3`, `spk2info.pt`, and for v2/v3 the `CosyVoice-BlankEN` config and tokenizer (not its weights, which `llm.pt` replaces). The shared asset `cosyvoice/wetext` holds the text normaliser's FSTs. The ONNX models are converted once and cached as `<model>/.mizuoto/converted-<key>.safetensors` (a `<name>.safetensors` beside the ONNX file wins)."],[12363,"The variant from the folder's files only, without torch"],[11410,"the version: flash-attn ≥ 2.6; xFormers outside 0.0.21–0.0.26 (broken for large batches) and with its C++ kernels (`_has_cpp_library`: a wheel for another torch imports without them);"],[10644,"The versions of Mizuoto, Python and the main components (torch, fastapi, uvicorn, pydantic, typer, httpx, numpy, av, `mizuoto-fishspeech`, `mizuoto-indextts`; a component that is not installed has no version). Option: `--json`."],[8588,"The voice library"],[10784,"The voice library"],[11774,"The voice library (folders), fit, design, export/import"],[16999,"The voice library, one folder per voice"],[9921,"The voice library, reference clips and voice caches"],[9165,"The voice library: `list_voices`, `get`, `create_from_audio`"],[16702,"The voice library: make voices from audio, design them, add preset speakers, manage clips, transcripts and fine-tuned weights, see which models can use them, export and import."],[16780,"The voice library: make, design, import and export voices, and see which models can use them"],[16824,"The voice library: voices from clips (speech recognition fills in missing transcripts), designed voices, preset speakers and voices with their own fine-tuned weights; export and import."],[15174,"The voice prompt is made from the reference three times over: 16 kHz audio to a Whisper log-mel to the **speech tokenizer**'s tokens; 16 kHz audio to a kaldi fbank to **CAM++**'s 192-dim speaker embedding; and always a 24 kHz Matcha mel, even for the 22.05 kHz CosyVoice 1. The **language model** turns text (and the prompt's text and tokens) into speech tokens; the **flow** turns tokens into a mel in 10 Euler steps with guidance 0.7; **HiFT** (a HiFi-GAN with a neural source filter and an inverse STFT) turns the mel into audio."],[10180,"The voice, described"],[10278,"The voice, described"],[16197,"The voice: **Library voice**, **Preset speaker** or **Its own voice**, as the model supports. The library picker shows how this model can use each voice, as in Speak."],[16544,"the voice's GPT and SoVITS weights"],[10259,"The voice's language"],[10253,"The voice's name"],[10274,"The voice's name"],[16705,"The voice's page"],[15727,"The VoxCPM engine as implemented in Mizuoto: VoxCPM2, 1.5 and 0.5B, MiniCPM-4, the local DiT and the AudioVAE, the tokenizer and normaliser as upstream's locked libraries build them, what reproduces upstream exactly, patch decoding with CUDA graphs, the full and LoRA fine-tunes, and its parity results."],[11496,"The waits were removed with exact equivalents of upstream's idioms (masked assignments, list indices, Python scalars stored into tensors, `.item()` checks), and the stop flag is read once per step. `dispatch.DEBUG`'s mask check is skipped while a stream captures (it reads back; the warm-up checked)."],[12715,"The warm request before the CPU rounds:"],[12699,"The warm runs of two rounds side by side, the speed-up, the time to first audio of streamed cases and the phases that changed most"],[15070,"The WAV is read as soundfile reads it (channels averaged) and resampled to 16 kHz by soxr (its HQ default)."],[10537,"The ways a model can be fine-tuned, with their stages and hyperparameters"],[14356,"The web UI (`mizuoto/webui/`) and the docs site (`site/`) use bun to install, build and test. `dev.py` looks for `bun` on `PATH`, then in the installer's default `~/.bun/bin`, and gives a clear error, not a traceback, when neither has it."],[14910,"The web UI is a Vue 3 project in `mizuoto/webui/`. Its components are Material Web (`@material/web`), its icons Lucide (`@lucide/vue`), its data layer TanStack Query (`@tanstack/vue-query`) with `openapi-fetch`, its state Pinia. The build, `mizuoto/webui/dist/`, ships in the wheel as package data and is served by the API's `SPAStaticFiles` (see HTTP API and command line). The base (`theme/`, `ui/`, motion, layers, the shell, stores, i18n, rule tests) is rvc-next's; where it comes from is in Design references and decisions."],[9677,"The web UI opens on **Speak**, where the dummy engine works right away (it speaks in tones); there is no setup screen. Choose the download source under **Settings** › **Downloads**, check torch under **Settings** › **Compute** (or with `mizuoto doctor`), then download models from **Models**, or with the button that replaces **Speak** when the chosen model is not downloaded, and follow them in **Jobs**. See First run."],[8862,"The web UI, built with bun (`mizuoto/webui/dist`)"],[9925,"The web UI, the HTTP API, the command line"],[14331,"The web UI: bun"],[9235,"The web UI's address, the port, whether it serves"],[16764,"The web UI's layout: navigation, the jobs sheet, the models in memory, the theme, and the guide to each screen."],[14059,"The weights in ONNX files are converted into torch modules by an in-tree protobuf reader (`runtime/convert/onnx.py`), the result cached under the model folder's `.mizuoto/`"],[16753,"The weights' version is read from the files. GPT-SoVITS models of the same version switch to these weights when they use the voice (marked **own weights** under **Which models can use it**); models of another version warn and clone as usual. **The voice keeps its clips too: the engine still needs a reference clip with the weights.** Weights exported by a training experiment are added to the voice for you."],[12196,"The Whisper encoder lives in the ASR engine and is not shared with CosyVoice's speech tokenizers"],[12945,"The whole S2 Pro through the stack (`perf.py`, `cases/fishspeech.jsonl`), on a free RTX 3060 12 GB (driver 595, torch 2.8.0+cu128, bf16, commit `c422e58`), nothing else on the machine; the faster of three warm runs, seconds:"],[15074,"The windows' tokens are merged into text and timestamped segments by the pipeline's `_decode_asr`."],[9835,"The working memory set aside for a step follows the request: a language model's cache is sized by the text, not by the longest generation `max_new_tokens` allows. A generation that runs far longer than its text and outgrows the GPU runs that step again with more weights streamed, with the same result."],[12169,"Their licences (Fish Audio Research License, bilibili Model Use License) cover the code; a port is a derivative, and folding it into the GPL-3.0 `mizuoto` would conflict"],[9371,"Their results cannot be added to another engine's training datasets"],[14989,"Theme, seed colour, contrast, language, motion, last screen, Speak's last choices; kept in localStorage and synced to the server through `/api/v1/client-state/{key}`, so they follow the user across browsers"],[10864,"Then allow an engine's cheaper way (tiles, smaller batches; the output differs slightly)"],[8804,"Then binary messages: mono 16-bit little-endian PCM at the `star