part not bit-exact: it differs from onnxruntime's by at most 7e-6 (cosine 0.999999999997). The flow turns that into a mel change of at most 2.7e-3, and HiFT's sine source integrates the F0 into phase (a float32 cumulative sum over the whole utterance, nine harmonics), so the error grows along the utterance: on a CosyVoice 3 English clone the SNR per half second falls from 66 to 20 dB. Upstream is just as sensitive. Its own vocoder chain fed Mizuoto's embedding gives exactly Mizuoto's audio; its own onnxruntime CAM++ with 8 threads instead of 1 gives 31 dB; random perturbations of that size give 20–33 dB. CosyVoice 2/3's language model never uses the speaker embedding, so the speech tokens are the same."],[15094,"Through the stack, `scripts/parity/cases/asr.jsonl` (seven clips, 4–120 s, English, Chinese and mixed, language detected or given) gives 0.1's transcripts exactly on the CPU in fp32 and on a GPU (an RTX 3090, 2026-10-19): language, text and every segment's timestamps."],[13012,"Through the whole stack on the GPU (`perf.py --device cuda:0`), best warm run:"],[15224,"Through the whole stack, results agree closely but not bit for bit with upstream, because CAM++ is not bit-exact with onnxruntime."],[14503,"Tier"],[15882,"Tier"],[15818,"Tiers"],[14409,"Tiers and tolerances of behavioural consistency"],[12226,"Tiled decoding as an out-of-memory fallback only for some decoders (ASR, GPT-SoVITS, F5-TTS's Vocos, Fish Speech's codec, IndexTTS 2's BigVGAN, OmniVoice's audio tokenizer, VoxCPM's VAE)"],[10026,"Time allowed to connect and complete the handshake"],[14489,"Time the same cases and fine-tunes phase by phase and check the audio, metrics and weights against the previous round (see Performance work)"],[10020,"Timeouts:"],[14405,"Tiny random models"],[10005,"TLS on one side only"],[1481,"TLS 设置不一致"],[12029,"To add"],[15978,"To clone a voice, models usually need the reference clip's transcript. With the speech recognition model downloaded, missing transcripts are