including their training/inference mismatches (Qwen3-TTS's training skips `text_projection`; Fish Speech's training does not scale the codebook embeddings by 1/√11)"],[9270,"Training"],[11137,"Training"],[12455,"Training"],[15132,"Training"],[15234,"Training"],[15290,"Training"],[15405,"Training"],[15497,"Training"],[15596,"Training"],[15657,"Training"],[15733,"Training"],[15830,"Training"],[16270,"Training"],[16850,"Training"],[9927,"Training (always here)"],[16571,"Training always runs on this machine, never on a remote host; when an engine's device is on a remote host, its methods are not available. A fine-tune takes its device for itself while it runs. Choose the device under **Settings › Training › Training device**; by default it is **The engine’s device**."],[8603,"Training datasets"],[10796,"Training experiments"],[9879,"Training has its own setting, `training.attention` (**Settings** › **Training** › **Attention**). It offers only backends with a backward pass, so not SageAttention."],[14772,"Training methods in the manifest"],[16570,"Training needs nothing beyond Mizuoto and torch: every method runs in Mizuoto's own Python, each stage in a process of its own. Some methods need shared files used only for training, such as GPT-SoVITS's pretrained discriminators (`mizuoto asset download gptsovits/s2d-v2pro`). When something is missing, the new-experiment dialog marks the method **not available** and gives the command to run."],[11051,"Training precision: `auto`, `fp32`, `fp16`, `bf16`"],[14284,"Training stages are the one exception: they run in their own process and seed the process-wide generators there (see Trainers)."],[12640,"Training stages run in their own process and own their device: before a GPU stage the host moves every idle model off that GPU, and the train job holds every slot of `gpu:<dev>` (`JobSpec.exclusive`). Inside the stage, `training.memory` chooses a preset of `mizuoto/training/memory.py`'s tools; a method's own hyperparameters win:"],[14840,"Training starts from a dataset. A dataset is `datasets/<slug>/`: `dataset.json`, `manifest.jsonl` (one row per clip: `id`, `audio`, `text`, `speaker`, `language`, `duration`, the rate, `excluded`, the source and `licence_tags`) and `audio/<id>.flac` (at most 48 kHz). The dataset's fingerprint is the SHA-256 of `manifest.jsonl`."],[12490,"Training tools"],[14797,"Training-only shared assets per variant (GPT-SoVITS's pretrained discriminators); `\"*\"` for every variant"],[12830,"Training, one fine-tune per trainer (s), metrics and weight tensors identical (the stages get the CPU settings through their environment):"],[14882,"Training's memory presets (`training.memory`: `standard`, `low`, `lowest`) and tools are in `mizuoto/training/memory.py`: gradient checkpointing puts back the global generators and the trainer's own during the backward recomputation, so losses and weights do not change; `low` adds only tools that keep results, `lowest` also those that change them slightly; a method's own hyperparameters win. A stage on a GPU adds `memory/peak_mb` to its metrics, and `MethodInfo.memory_mb` estimates a run's peak per preset. Details in Memory management."],[14485,"Trains on the workspace's dataset with one implementation and keeps the experiment, metrics, previews and exports"],[10227,"Transcribe a clip with the speech recognition engine."],[10965,"Transcribe a reference clip without a transcript (needs the speech recognition model `tts.asr_model` downloaded)"],[10320,"Transcribe the clips (or this one) again with speech recognition"],[11136,"Transcribe, convert and edit"],[16402,"Transcripts and speech recognition"],[9642,"Transcripts are cached by the audio's SHA-256, the model and the beam width, so the same clip is never transcribed twice with the same settings. `tts.auto_transcribe` (on by default), `tts.asr_model` and `tts.asr_beams` (5 by default) control automatic transcription; see Configuration."],[9332,"transcripts for reference clips and datasets"],[11768,"Transcripts through the `asr` engine, cached by audio SHA-256 and model"],[4557,"transformer 0.90"],[13081,"transformer 0.90"],[4207,"transformer 69.7"],[12731,"transformer 69.7"],[14056,"transformers (several incompatible versions), accelerate, huggingface_hub, peft, loralib"],[15919,"transformers' logits processors in their order; `multinomial`'s own computation without its device waits"],[5532,"transformers（多个互不兼容的版本）、accelerate、huggingface_hub、peft、loralib"],[14002,"Truncating VoxCPM's attention to exactly the filled positions: identical in bf16, not in fp32 (the kernel's blocks change); the cut at a multiple of 256 is identical in both."],[16709,"Try it"],[68,"tts"],[8592,"tts"],[16204,"Two buttons at the bottom of the page:"],[15878,"Two engines have another reference:"],[16892,"Two helper engines are built in as well: **speech recognition** (Whisper large-v3-turbo, which fills in the transcripts of reference clips) and the **dummy engine** (`dummy/default`, nothing to download; it speaks in tones so you can learn the UI first)."],[15635,"Two phases: the audio tokenizer (the voice prompt, then decoding) and the language model. If decoding runs out of memory with `compute.oom_fallback` on, the tokenizer decodes in tiles of 128 frames (about 5 s), each with the 12 frames its DAC decoder's samples depend on each side: the whole's samples up to the sums' rounding (64 dB SNR on a GPU, where the GPU against the CPU is 63 dB), in 108 MB instead of 1 GB for 60 s. The language model reruns over the whole sequence each step, so it is a `oneshot` model for weight streaming (its largest units stay on the device). Training: gradient checkpointing over the model's layers is identical, LoRA dropout included; `lowest` keeps AdamW's state in RAM (identical on the CPU)."],[15272,"Two phases: the transformer with the mel (every ODE step; guidance doubles the batch) and Vocos. If Vocos runs out of memory with `compute.oom_fallback` on, it decodes in tiles of 256 frames, each with the 29 frames its samples depend on each side (its kernels and the inverse STFT's window): the whole's samples up to the sums' rounding (`applied.fallbacks` says so)."],[9893,"Two settings make CPU work faster without changing any result (Linux; on other systems they change nothing):"],[15301,"Two variants. `s2_pro` (catalogue model `fishspeech/s2-pro`, this page up to Drama 3): cloning from one to four clips, each with its transcript; inline tags; dialogue between speakers (`<|speaker:i|>`). The model folder holds `config.json`, the weights (`model.safetensors.index.json` and its shards, `model.safetensors`, or `model.pth`), `codec.pth` and the BPE tokenizer files. A voice's cache is `codes.pt`, each reference's codes."],[14355,"ty does not follow an editable install's path hook, so `pyproject.toml` sets `tool.ty.environment.extra-paths` to `packages/native/fishspeech` and `packages/native/indextts`, which resolves `mizuoto_fishspeech` and `mizuoto_indextts` from source. torch and the optional extras' packages are listed in `tool.ty.analysis.allowed-unresolved-imports`."],[14368,"ty over `mizuoto`, the gated engines, `tests` and `scripts`"],[5831,"ty 不跟随可编辑安装的路径钩子，所以 `pyproject.toml` 把 `tool.ty.environment.extra-paths` 设为 `packages/native/fishspeech` 和 `packages/native/indextts`，从源码解析 `mizuoto_fishspeech` 和 `mizuoto_indextts`。torch 和各可选附加依赖的包列在 `tool.ty.analysis.allowed-unresolved-imports` 里。"],[12390,"Type"],[17037,"Type anything under **Text**."],[16573,"Type the **Dataset name**, choose the **Language**, and optionally a **Description**."],[16024,"Type the **Name of the new voice** to put it in the library"],[16485,"Type the **Name of the new voice** to put it in the library"],[16117,"Type the **Project name**."],[16445,"Type the clip's text under **What is said in the clip**. **Transcribe** has speech recognition fill it in now, for you to correct."],[3757,"Typer 的限制；`--preset` 先被说话人占用"],[11693,"typer, click, rich, pydantic, uvicorn, httpx"],[3169,"typer、click、rich、pydantic、uvicorn、httpx"],[12281,"Typer's limit; `--preset` was taken by speakers first"],[14962,"Types come from `api/types.ts`: `S = components['schemas']` plus aliases for the common models. Models used both as request and response are split, e.g. send `S['SpeakRequest-Input']`, read `S['SpeakRequest-Output']`."],[11528,"Types for the web UI"],[12112,"Types generated at build time only"],[12056,"Types: `feat` (a feature), `fix`, `perf` (faster with the same results), `refactor` (no change in behaviour), `test`, `docs`, `build` (builds, CI, Docker), `chore`. A breaking change adds `!` after the type, as in `refactor!:`."],[11157,"Typical cause"],[6241,"Ubuntu"],[14765,"Ubuntu"],[14762,"Ubuntu, bun"],[14756,"Ubuntu, Python 3.11, bun"],[14759,"Ubuntu, Python 3.11, bun, Playwright's Chromium (`playwright install --with-deps chromium`)"],[14753,"Ubuntu, Python 3.12, torch 2.8.0 and the latest release"],[14744,"Ubuntu, Windows, macOS × Python 3.10, 3.11, 3.12, 3.13, 3.14"],[6238,"Ubuntu、bun"],[6232,"Ubuntu、Python 3.11、bun"],[6235,"Ubuntu、Python 3.11、bun、Playwright 的 Chromium（`playwright install --with-deps chromium`）"],[6229,"Ubuntu、Python 3.12，torch 2.8.0 和最新版"],[6220,"Ubuntu、Windows、macOS × Python 3.10、3.11、3.12、3.13、3.14"],[10740,"UI"],[10777,"UI"],[10813,"UI"],[10918,"UI"],[10946,"UI"],[11044,"UI"],[11076,"UI"],[11004,"UI (engine card)"],[12100,"UI preferences are stored on the server through `/api/v1/client-state/{key}`, so they follow the user across browsers."],[14707,"unchanged"],[16508,"Under **Changes**, fill in **The whole text after the edit**: everything the recording should say once edited. The easy way: click **Transcribe** to transcribe the recording, then change the words you replace. The model reads this text."],[16376,"Under **Folders**, these can be moved elsewhere, each showing its default location: **Models**, **Voices**, **Results**, **Cache**. Empty means the default place in the data folder."],[17035,"Under **Model**, choose **Du