 speech recognition"],[9066,"Uploading to Hugging Face uses `hf upload`, which splits a large folder into several commits and resumes when run again (`hf upload-large-folder` with a `huggingface_hub` older than 2); it needs the `huggingface_hub` command line, after `hf auth login`; ModelScope needs the `modelscope` command line. The folder must hold a `MIRROR.json`."],[11759,"Uploads, references (registered by content)"],[15719,"Upstream adds the raw text embedding to the codec embeddings without its `text_projection`, which inference applies; kept, so the weights are upstream's. It follows that only a model whose text embeddings are as wide as the talker can train: the 1.7B Base can, the 0.6B Base cannot (text 2048, talker 1024). The method shows as unavailable for such a model, with the reason, and an experiment cannot start from it (`Trainer.refuses` reads the model's `config.json` before a run; `capability_not_supported`)."],[12205,"Upstream pins wetext 0.1.2, whose FSTs differ from both CosyVoice's and IndexTTS's"],[14891,"Upstream reseeds everything with its config's seed after building the model; the native trainer makes those later draws on private generators seeded the same way (the data-loader workers' seeds, the LoRA dropout masks), while the LoRA initialisation draws from the stage process's global generator in module order, as upstream does; so a seeded run gives upstream's losses and weights."],[12203,"Upstream's accelerated path changes results; replaying the eager kernels does not"],[15260,"Upstream's bundled vocabulary"],[12188,"Upstream's quirks are reproduced first and fixes land as separate changes; even quirks of no product value are reproduced (IndexTTS-1.5 using no KV cache below fp16)"],[11840,"Usage is in Remote hosts; the client side in Runtime."],[14229,"Use"],[16428,"Use"],[9688,"use another GPU: `mizuoto config set engines.<id>.device cuda:1` (**Models** › **Engines** › **Device**);"],[9797,"use at most this much of each GPU (MB; `0`: al