ce. When that is not enough, and `compute.oom_fallback` is on, an engine with a cheaper way uses it (speech recognition one 30 s window at a time, GPT-SoVITS one text at a time, F5-TTS's, Fish Speech's, IndexTTS's, OmniVoice's and VoxCPM's decoders in tiles). Otherwise the request fails with `compute_unavailable` (`detail.reason` is `out_of_memory`), and, as ComfyUI does, Mizuoto unloads every model not in use from every GPU, so the next try starts on empty devices (models on the CPU stay). If it fails again, give the engine another device, set `compute.vram_mode` to `low` or `none`, or lower `compute.max_resident_models`. Mizuoto also remembers how much memory each step really used and sets that much aside the next time."],[9812,"when a step runs out of GPU memory, run it again with more of its weights in RAM: the same result, slower"],[12228,"When a training run's estimated memory exceeds the free memory, the log warns with the preset that would fit; the run is not refused"],[16425,"When all is done the **Speak** button is back."],[9719,"When an engine fails, the request fails with `engine_error` (exit code 10), whose detail carries the exception and its traceback (**Details** under the error in the web UI; the job's `error` in `mizuoto job show <job id> --json`). The **Models in memory** panel lists an engine whose last request failed, with the error."],[16076,"When an engine has load options, its card has **Options**:"],[14314,"When an engine's device is `<host>/<device>` (for example `engines.qwen3tts.device = \"gpu-box/cuda:0\"`), `RuntimeService.engine` asks `RemoteService` for a `RemoteEngine`: a session with the `mizuoto agent` on that host for one engine on one device. The agent is a whole Mizuoto with its own data folder, models and runtime; it runs the engine in its own process exactly as a host does. `RemoteEngineHandle` answers the same calls as `LocalHandle`. For the user-facing set-up, see Remote engines."],[9707,"When every source fails the job ends with `download_failed` (exit code 12), whose detail lists the sources tried and the last errors."],[12564,"When free memory falls short, idle components on the same device give up the shortfall, in this order:"],[8803,"When generation starts: `{\"type\": \"start\", \"job_id\": …, \"sample_rate\": 24000, \"granularity\": \"token\" | \"segment\" | \"emulated\"}`."],[9691,"When memory runs out during a request anyway, Mizuoto runs the step again with more of its weights in RAM and the same random draws (the same result, slower); with `compute.oom_fallback` it then tries a cheaper way (tiles, smaller batches). `compute.gpu_jobs` (default 1) sets how many jobs run at once on one GPU; a job waiting for the GPU can be started beside the running one with **Run anyway** when the memory suffices. `compute.inference_jobs` (default 1) sets how many synthesis jobs run at once across all engines and devices. More in Performance."],[9915,"When one machine has the GPU and another is where you use Mizuoto, an engine can run on the GPU machine. That machine runs `mizuoto agent` (the **agent** below); the machine you use (the **host** below) adds it as a remote host and sets the engine's device to `<name>/<device>`, for example `gpu-box/cuda:0`. Synthesis, streaming and cancelling then work as they do locally; only the engine, and the models it loads, run on the agent."],[10999,"When requests are batched: Performance."],[9912,"When something fails"],[9654,"When something goes wrong, read the job's log first (**Log** in the **Jobs** panel, or `mizuoto job log <job id>`), then run `mizuoto doctor`: it checks torch's build against the hardware, whether each engine is available and which optional extras are missing, and gives the commands that fix what it finds."],[16515,"When something is missing the footer says so: **Add the recording**, **Give the text after the edit**, or **Mark what to replace: from and to, in seconds**."],[12050,"When the API changes, regenerate the types and commit them, or `typegen-check` fails. UI changes pass the rule tests (imports, tokens, layout, layers, i18n keys)."],[16797,"When the chosen model is not ready yet, the main button is replaced by the one step it still needs — **Enable**, **Accept the** *engine* **licence**, the command that installs what the engine needs (torch, or a licence-gated engine's package) or **Download** *model* *(size)* — with its progress while it runs."],[17042,"When the download is done the **Speak** button is back. Pick a **Preset speaker**, optionally write an instruction under **Style** › **How to say it** (such as \"Cheerfully, a little faster\"), and click **Speak**."],[16066,"when the file sizes match a catalogue model, it checks their SHA-256 and imports the folder as that model;"],[8991,"When the file sizes match a catalogue model's manifest exactly, the folder becomes that catalogue model and every file's SHA-256 is then checked; a mismatch is an error."],[9246,"When the host program is itself a FastAPI (or other ASGI) application, it can mount Mizuoto instead of opening another port:"],[16398,"When the model is not ready"],[16635,"When the result is a voice's weights, **Voice to give the weights**: a library voice, or **A new voice** (made from three of the dataset's clips of 3 to 10 seconds)."],[17028,"When the server is ready the terminal prints `SERVER_READY url=http://127.0.0.1:7869`, and a browser opens that address a moment later. The default port is **7869**, and only this machine can connect by default. Press Ctrl+C to stop the server."],[16064,"When you already have a model's files (an earlier download, a copy from elsewhere, a fine-tune), click **Import a model folder** and choose a folder on the server. The button shows only in a browser on the server machine."],[16700,"When you pick a method for a new experiment, the dialog shows roughly how much GPU memory a run needs with each Memory setting; the experiment's page shows, in **GPU memory**, the free memory of the GPU