for a long time unless a wheel matches the torch, and its only wheel for torch 2.8 stops xFormers 0.0.32 from importing. Choose them under Settings › Compute › Acceleration."],[9242,"With `api_prefix=\"/voice\"` the web UI is at `<address>/voice/`, the API at `/voice/api/v1/...` and the OpenAI-compatible API at `/voice/v1/...`. The web UI derives the prefix from its own script's URL; nothing else to configure."],[12867,"With `compute.attention = fast` on the CPU every call goes through the policy, all on SDPA, no fallbacks (calls per request: F5-TTS 704, OmniVoice 896, GPT-SoVITS v4 3,044, VoxCPM 1.5 3,928, CosyVoice 2 4,688, Qwen3-TTS 4,877, IndexTTS 2 6,667, Fish Speech 7,152). Seven engines still gave identical audio; IndexTTS 2 differed by at most 2 int16 steps (86.1 dB SNR, same length), its perceiver's hand-written softmax being computed by SDPA."],[15377,"With `compute.cuda_graphs` (an NVIDIA GPU holding the backbone and the tower whole: about 44 GB in bfloat16) the decoding step runs as CUDA graphs that replay the eager kernels (`drama3/steps.py`, `generate.Decoder`). A step is the tower's graphs (the output head, the frame's draws, one graph between each two of its 13 layers' attention calls), then the backbone's on that frame (one graph between each two of its 10 softmax attention layers, the Gated DeltaNet layers, the router and the experts inside them). The attention calls run eagerly between the graphs, over caches that grow by one each step, so the caches and the attention kernels are the eager code's. The step waits for the device once, for the frame's main token and whether its logits were finite."],[15796,"With `compute.cuda_graphs` (NVIDIA, the model wholly on its device, `compute.compile` off) a patch is one CUDA graph per number of steps and guidance value (the attention span is the whole cache there); the DiT's noise is drawn from the graphs' generator, loaded from the request's and written back at each patch. The language models' static caches are then kept with the model while graphs are kept (the memory a request needs anyway) and go when the weights move or the model unloads. The real 0.5B and 1.5 give the same audio with and without graphs, 1.6–1.9 times faster per request."],[15335,"With `compute.cuda_graphs` (NVIDIA, the model wholly on its device) `generate.Decoder` keeps fixed tensors per loaded model: the slow step runs as one graph per stretch between attention calls (`LayerSteps`), and the frame's draws, repetition-aware sampling and the fast transformer as one graph. The sampling settings are device tensors filled per request, so one set of graphs serves every request. The codes are identical, 2.2–2.5 times faster per frame on the decode loop."],[9839,"With `compute.vram_mode = high` (**Whole or not at all**), Mizuoto always tries to load a model whole, whatever the catalogue's estimate and the card's free memory say, as ComfyUI does. It first moves idle models off that GPU to make room, then copies the weights. The request fails only when an allocation really fails: the code is `compute_unavailable` (`detail.reason` is `out_of_memory`; exit code 9 on the command line), and every model not in use is then unloaded from every GPU (see below). With `compute.gpu_jobs` above 1, a request short of room while another request holds the GPU first waits for it to finish (up to 10 minutes), then tries."],[8954,"With `downloads.repository` set to `mizuoto-model` (the default), the mizuoto-model mirror first;"],[8960,"With `downloads.verify_checksums` (**Verify checksums**, on by default) off, only sizes are checked."],[9673,"With `server.access_token` set, the UI shows the **Access token** dialog (\"This server asks for its access token.\"); enter it once. An API request without it gets 401 `auth_required`; send it as an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header, the `mizuoto_token` cookie or a `?token=` query parameter (see HTTP API)."],[11888,"With `tts.micro_batch` on, `TtsService._batch_group()` gives a speak job a `JobSpec.group` when the variant has the `batch` capability with `max_batch > 1`, the request has one segment, no seed (a batch draws its random numbers differently) and does not stream. The group is a hash of everything but the text. Just before calling the engine, the running job calls `JobContext.adopt(max_batch - 1)`, which takes the oldest queued jobs of its group, and sends one `SynthesisTask` whose `texts` hold every text; the engine yields text *i*'s chunks with `segment = i`, the job stores one output per job and ends the adopted ones with `complete()` / `fail()`. If the batched call fails, they are `release()`d to the queue and each runs on its own."],[10016,"With a hint to run `mizuoto doctor <engine>` on the agent"],[10032,"With a self-signed agent certificate, give that certificate as `--ca-file` on the host; the host name in the certificate is then not checked. Without `--ca-file` the system's CAs are used."],[12625,"With half the context (or one frame) the seams differ visibly, which the tests check. Qwen3-TTS's codec already decodes in chunks; CosyVoice's HiFT carries a phase that tiles would break. `tiled_1d` (overlapping tiles, cross-faded, as ComfyUI tiles audio VAEs) is no longer used by an engine here; it stays for released engine packages that call it."],[12554,"With host copies (`compute.host_copies`: `auto` keeps them while free RAM stays above `compute.ram_reserve_mb`; `on`; `off`), a parameter placed on the device keeps its host tensor, so offloading it costs no transfer: the device is a cache over RAM. A partly loaded component always keeps them (its streamed units rest there). Buffers are always copied back (a module may update one in place)."],[12277,"With it, every defaulted response field would become optional in the generated types; the split it avoids only touches `SpeakRequest`"],[15960,"With Mizuoto installed and `mizuoto webui` running, this page takes you through the first use: where to start, checking torch and the engines, what a model download does, the licence-gated engines, and finally the first synthesis. Each step is given for the web UI and the command line."],[16029,"With more than one result listed, **Download all** downloads them together."],[16490,"With more than one result, **Download all** downloads them together."],[8772,"With neither `voice` nor `voice_spec`, the model speaks in its own voice (if it has one). To check a request without running it, `POST /api/v1/tts/plan` returns the segments, the parameters that apply and the warnings. A top-level field the request does not have is ignored, so that a client sending a newer version's field keeps working, and named in the warnings (\"Ignored fields the request does not have: …\"): engine options go in `engine_options`, and `options` there would be ignored. A conversion or an edit logs such fields."],[9086,"With several machines on a local network, one machine's models can be laid out as a mirror for the others. The URLs Mizuoto requests from a custom endpoint have this form:"],[14714,"within 0.004"],[14715,"within 0.03"],[12829,"within the noise"],[11208,"Without `-m`, `tts.default_model` is used. `mizuoto model spec <model>` lists the voice modes, languages, common parameters and engine options a model takes."],[8774,"Without a `transcript`, speech recognition fills it in when `tts.auto_transcribe` is on and the recognition model is downloaded; otherwise the model must clone without one. To keep the voice, add it to the library (`POST /api/v1/voices`) and name it with `\"voice\": \"<id>\"`."],[15071,"Without a language, the language is detected on the first 30 s (one decoder step over the language tokens)."],[14050,"Without an extra, text in that language fails with `capability_not_supported` and the install command in the hint; `mizuoto doctor` lists each engine's missing extras too. The optional attention packages (flash-attn, xFormers, SageAttention) are not extras: they must match the user's torch, and `mizuot